add('reading-format','base:152,153,154,175,178,179,188,195 extra:45,207',
 'Academic Reading odatda uchta uzun matn; General Training esa kundalik va ish hayoti matnlari bilan uch bo‘limdan tuziladi. Ikkalasida 40 savol va jami 60 daqiqa bor. Mashqda 18–20 daqiqalik bo‘lakdan boshlang, qiyin savolni belgilab keyingisiga o‘ting va tekshirishga vaqt qoldiring. Saytdagi aniq test hajmini uning yo‘riqnomasidan tekshiring.',
 'Academic Reading uses three long texts; General Training uses three sections with everyday and workplace material. Both have 40 questions in 60 minutes. Practise in 18–20-minute blocks, move past a stuck question, and leave checking time. Check the specific site task instructions as practice sets may differ.')
add('reading-method','base:162,167,168,180,183,190,194,196 extra:201,202,203,215,216,264',
 'Avval savol talabini aniqlang. Skimming — matnning umumiy fikrini tez tushunish; scanning — ism, sana yoki kerakli faktni qidirish. Topilgan joyning oldingi-keyingi gapini diqqat bilan o‘qing: bir xil so‘zning o‘zi dalil emas. Har savol turi ketma-ket kelavermaydi. Masalan: 1) heading uchun paragraf maqsadi; 2) sana uchun raqam; 3) sabab uchun because/since va ma’no bog‘lanishini tekshiring.',
 'Identify what the question asks. Skimming finds the overall message; scanning locates a name, date or detail. Read the surrounding sentences closely: a repeated keyword alone is not proof. Not every task type follows text order. For example, seek paragraph purpose for headings, a number for dates, and the meaning of causal links for reasons.')
add('completed-review','base:165,166,181,182,185,191,192,193,198,200,222,223,242,243,247 extra:206,212,213,219,230',
 'Tahlil uchun savol, sizning javobingiz va tegishli gap yoki tugallangan urinish kerak. Xatoni uch tomondan ko‘ramiz: dalilni topish, ma’noni tushunish, format/imlo. Faqat o‘zingizga ochilgan yakunlangan test izohini ishlataman; yopiq kalitni taxmin qilmayman. Savol matnini yoki ruxsat etilgan natija sahifasidagi izohni yozing.',
 'Review needs the question, your answer and the relevant passage or completed attempt. We can separate errors in locating evidence, understanding meaning, and formatting/spelling. Only released feedback for an authorised completed attempt may be used; I will not infer a hidden key. Share the question or permitted result explanation.',kind='clarify')
add('word-limit','base:186,209,210,232,233',
 'Yo‘riqnomadagi so‘z va raqam chegarasiga aynan rioya qiling. «ONE WORD ONLY» — bitta so‘z; ortiqcha so‘z javobni yaroqsiz qilishi mumkin. Imlo va gapga grammatik moslikni ham tekshiring. Masalan: 1) school — bitta so‘z; 2) primary school — ikki so‘z; 3) 15 May — bitta raqam va bitta so‘z. Javob formatini faqat katta harf yozish bilan tuzatib bo‘lmaydi.',
 'Follow the exact word/number limit and check spelling and grammatical fit. ONE WORD ONLY permits one word; an extra word may invalidate an answer. For example: school is one word, primary school is two, and 15 May is one number plus one word. Capitalisation alone cannot fix a wrong answer.')
add('exam-boundary','base:177,197,206,237,240,248,249,451,452,455,456,457,458,459,461,462,463,464,480,481,482,483,489,493,494,591,592,594,595 extra:25,26,190,220',
 'Practice va baholanadigan imtihonning yordami bir xil emas. Mashqda usul va ruxsatli matnni o‘rganamiz; faol yoki yopiq imtihonda tayyor javob, kalit yoki sizning o‘rningizga topshirishni bermayman. Boshlash, qayta urinish, audio va taymer qoidalarini aynan o‘sha test yo‘riqnomasidan tekshiring. Umumiy yechish strategiyasini tushuntira olaman.',
 'Practice and graded exams allow different kinds of assistance. Practice may include methods and permitted text; I cannot provide active or unreleased exam keys or submit work for you. Starting, retrying, audio and timer rules must be checked in that task’s instructions. I can explain general strategies.')
add('listening-format','base:202,203,204,205,215,216,217,246',
 'Listening to‘rt qism va jami 40 savoldan iborat. Dastlabki ikki qism kundalik vaziyatlar, keyingi ikkitasi o‘qish yoki ta’lim mavzularidir. Rasmiy test yozuvi bir marta eshittiriladi; saytdagi practice qayta tinglash qoidasi player va rejimga bog‘liq. Mashqda avval mustaqil tinglang, keyin xato joyini qayta eshitib sababini toping.',
 'Listening has four parts and 40 questions. The first two concern everyday settings; the last two concern education or training. Official recordings are played once. Replay in site practice depends on its mode and player. Attempt independently first, then replay difficult sections to identify the cause of an error.')
add('listening-method','base:218,220,221,224,225,226,227,228,229,231,244,245 extra:46,204,209,214,217,277',
 'Audio oldidan bo‘sh joy uchun qanday ma’no va so‘z turkumi kerakligini taxmin qiling. Tinglaganda o‘zgartirilgan fikrni ushlang: «Tuesday — sorry, Thursday» desa oxirgi tuzatish muhim. O‘tkazib yuborgan bitta javobda qolib ketmang. Mashqdan keyin: 1) xato qismini qayta eshiting; 2) ruxsatli transkript bilan solishtiring; 3) qiyin iborani aytib, yangi gapda ishlating.',
 'Before the audio, predict the meaning and word class needed. Listen for corrections: in Tuesday—sorry, Thursday, the final correction matters. Move on after a missed answer. After practice, replay the difficult section, compare an available transcript, then say the difficult phrase and use it in a new sentence.')
add('band-conversion','base:230,465,469,470,471',
 'Overall band — Listening, Reading, Writing va Speaking bandlarining o‘rtachasi, eng yaqin yarim bandga yaxlitlanadi. Masalan, o‘rtacha 6.25 bo‘lsa 6.5 bo‘ladi. Reading/Listening xom balli 40 savoldagi to‘g‘ri javoblar sonidir; aniq band chegarasi test va Reading turiga bog‘liq. Bitta xom ballni barcha testlar uchun kafolatli band deb ko‘rsatmang.',
 'The overall band is the average of the four skill bands, rounded to the nearest half band; 6.25 becomes 6.5. Reading and Listening raw scores count correct answers out of 40. Exact band thresholds depend on the test and Reading type, so a raw score is not a guaranteed band across all tests.')
add('writing-format','base:251,252,253,254,255,256,263,269,270,271,272,273,279,288,293,294,295 extra:226,239',
 'Academic Task 1 grafik, jadval yoki jarayonni kamida 150 so‘zda tasvirlaydi; Task 2 esa kamida 250 so‘zli insho. Jami 60 daqiqa: taxminan 20 va 40 daqiqa ajrating; Task 2 vazni kattaroq. Task 1’da ko‘rinadigan ma’lumotni taqqoslang, shaxsiy fikr qo‘shmang. Task 2’da savolning barcha qismlariga dalil va misol bilan javob bering. GT Task 1 — vaziyatga mos xat.',
 'Academic Task 1 describes visual information in at least 150 words; Task 2 is an essay of at least 250 words. There are 60 minutes: roughly 20 for Task 1 and 40 for Task 2, which carries more weight. Task 1 reports the data rather than personal opinions; Task 2 addresses every part with reasons and examples. General Training Task 1 is a letter.')
add('overview','base:257,292',
 'Overview — eng katta umumiy yo‘nalishlar, barcha raqamlar ro‘yxati emas. Avval nima oshgan/kamayganini yoki eng katta farqni tanlang, keyin tafsilotlarda dalil keltiring. Uchta namuna: 1) Overall, sales rose in both regions. — Umuman, ikkala hududda ham sotuv oshdi. 2) The north remained the largest market. — Shimol eng katta bozor bo‘lib qoldi. 3) In contrast, demand fell in the south. — Aksincha, janubda talab kamaydi. Bularni grafik ma’lumotiga mos bo‘lsagina ishlating.',
 'An overview selects major trends or contrasts, not every number. Example sentences: Overall, sales rose in both regions. The north remained the largest market. In contrast, demand fell in the south. These are invented practice examples; use a statement only when the actual chart supports it.')
add('writing-input','base:274,275,276,277,278,280,289,291,441,647 extra:78,112,154,157,221,222,223,224,225,227,228,229,231,232,233,235,236,237,238,240,258,313',
 'Savol sharti va o‘zingiz yozgan gap yoki paragrafni yuboring. Avval asosiy fikrni, keyin dalil va bog‘lanishni, oxirida grammatikani ko‘ramiz. Men asl ma’noni saqlab, aniq qoida bilgan joyimdagina tuzatish taklif qilaman; barcha matnni tekshirdim deb asossiz aytmayman. Faol baholanadigan ishni o‘rningizga yozmayman.',
 'Share the task and your own sentence or paragraph. We can check the main point, supporting evidence, links and grammar in that order. I preserve the intended meaning and suggest corrections only where supported; I cannot certify an entire text without adequate analysis. I do not replace your work in an active graded task.',kind='clarify')
add('writing-ui','base:281,283,284,285,298,472,475,476,485,486',
 'Tegishli Writing yoki natija sahifasini ochib, ko‘rsatilgan task, urinish va tekshirish statusini tekshiring. Filtr, so‘z sanagich, yuklab olish yoki qayta topshirish imkoniyati ko‘rinmasa, bor deb ayta olmayman. Qaysi sahifa va status ekanini yozing; xatoni natijani o‘zgartirmasdan tekshirish yo‘lini tanlaymiz.',
 'Open the relevant Writing or result page and check the task, attempt and review status. I cannot promise filtering, word counting, downloads or resubmission unless available there. Name the page and status so we can investigate without changing results.',kind='clarify')
add('writing-time','base:299,300 extra:47',
 '40 daqiqalik Task 2 mashqi: 5 daqiqa savol va reja, 30 daqiqa yozish, 5 daqiqa tekshirish. Rejada pozitsiya + ikkita asosiy sabab + har biriga bitta misol bo‘lsin. Tekshiruvda savolning barcha qismlariga javob, fe’l shakli va gap chegaralarini ko‘ring. Taymerni o‘zingiz boshlang; men uni ishga tushirdim deb aytmayman.',
 'For a 40-minute Task 2 practice, spend five minutes planning, thirty writing and five checking. Plan a position, two reasons and an example for each. Check task coverage, verb forms and sentence boundaries. Start your own timer; I have not started one for you.')
add('speaking-format','base:301,306,307,308,309,314,315,316,317,318,319,320,321,349',
 'Speaking’da Part 1 — shaxsiy va kundalik savollar; Part 2 — tayyorgarlikdan keyin uzunroq mustaqil javob; Part 3 — shu yo‘nalishdagi umumiyroq muhokama. Mashqda javob + sabab + misol bilan fikrni rivojlantiring. Tushunarlilik muhim; muayyan aksent yoki yodlangan murakkab so‘zning o‘zi yuqori band bermaydi. Matnli chat ovozli ijroni baholamaydi.',
 'Part 1 uses familiar personal questions, Part 2 an extended individual turn after preparation, and Part 3 a broader discussion. Practise an answer, a reason and an example. Intelligibility matters; an accent or memorised difficult word does not itself establish a high band. Text chat cannot assess spoken delivery.')
add('speaking-ui','base:310,311,325,326,327,329,330,341',
 'Speaking practice sahifasidagi savolni oching. Vocabulary, Ideas yoki Sample yordami ko‘rsatilgan bo‘lsa, uning tugmasi yo‘riqnomasiga amal qiling; namuna o‘zingizning hayotiy tajribangiz o‘rnini bosmaydi. Audio uchun aynan yozuv vositasi va mikrofon ruxsati kerak. RIWI’ga matn yozish audio yuborish bilan bir xil emas.',
 'Open a question in Speaking practice. Use Vocabulary, Ideas or Sample support only where shown and follow its control instructions. A sample does not replace your own experience. Audio requires the recording interface and microphone permission; typing in RIWI is not an audio submission.')
add('speaking-method','base:328,331,332,334,335,336,337,339,342,345,346,347,348 extra:48,145,159,242,243,244,246,247,248,251,252,253,255,260',
 'Yodlangan uzun skript o‘rniga fikrni kengaytirishni mashq qilamiz 🙂 Avval javob, keyin sabab, so‘ng bitta haqiqiy misol. 10 daqiqa: 2 daqiqa g‘oya, 3 daqiqa aytish, 3 daqiqa qayta tinglash/o‘qish, 2 daqiqa bir xatoni tuzatish. Boshlang: What do you enjoy doing in your free time, and why? Javobingizdan keyin keyingi savolni tanlaymiz.',
 'Practise developing an answer rather than memorising a long script: answer, reason, then a genuine example. In ten minutes, use two for ideas, three speaking, three reviewing and two fixing one issue. Start with: What do you enjoy doing in your free time, and why? We can choose a follow-up after your response.')
add('minimal-pairs','extra:249,250 base:394,638,639,640,641',
 'Talaffuzni ovoz bilan solishtirish kerak; matndan sizning talaffuzingizga ball qo‘ymayman. Uch juftlik: ship /ʃɪp/ — sheep /ʃiːp/; bit /bɪt/ — beat /biːt/; thin /θɪn/ — tin /tɪn/. Avval farqni tinglang, keyin bittadan ayting, yozuvni tekshiring. /θ/ uchun til uchi tishlar orasiga yaqin keladi, havo ishqalanib chiqadi; /t/ kabi to‘liq to‘xtamaydi.',
 'Pronunciation needs audio comparison; text does not establish your pronunciation score. Try ship /ʃɪp/ versus sheep /ʃiːp/, bit /bɪt/ versus beat /biːt/, and thin /θɪn/ versus tin /tɪn/. Listen, produce each word and review a recording. For /θ/, air passes with friction near the teeth rather than stopping as for /t/.')

add('vocabulary-ui','base:352,353,354,360,363,364,365,366,367,368,370,371,372,373,374,381,382,383,391,392,396,398,399',
 'Lug‘atda so‘zni alohida qidiring, so‘ng so‘z turkumi, ma’no va misolni matndagi vaziyat bilan solishtiring. Shaxsiy papka yoki o‘yin uchun faqat o‘sha sahifada bor boshqaruvdan foydalaning; ball formulasi yoki avtomatik importni ko‘rmasdan tasdiqlamayman. Qaysi so‘z va qaysi tugmada muammo borligini yozing. Bir so‘zning barcha ma’nolari bitta darajaga tegishli bo‘lavermaydi.',
 'Search the word and compare its part of speech, sense and example with your context. Use only controls actually offered for personal folders or games; I cannot verify scoring formulas or automatic imports without evidence. Name the word and the control involved. Different senses need not have the same learning level.')
add('cefr','base:355,356',
 'CEFR A1, A2, B1, B2, C1 va C2 darajalari tilni qanday ishlata olishingizni tasvirlaydi. Alohida so‘zdagi belgi butun darajangizni aniqlamaydi: masalan, oddiy so‘zning murakkab ma’nosi ham bor. So‘zni taniymanmi, kontekstda tushunamanmi va o‘zim gapda ishlata olamanmi — shu uch savol bilan tekshiring.',
 'CEFR levels A1 through C2 describe language-use ability. A label on one word does not determine your overall level, and a familiar word may have a more advanced sense. Check recognition, understanding in context and independent use.')
add('vocab-review','base:369,377,378,379,385 extra:36,37',
 'Bugun beshta kerakli so‘zni tanlang. Har biriga qisqa ma’no, tabiiy birikma va o‘zingiz haqingizda bitta gap yozing. Ertaga javobni yopib eslang; bir necha kundan keyin yangi gapda qo‘llang. Sinash uchun so‘zlaringizni yuboring — ma’no topish, bo‘sh joy va yangi gap tuzish savollarini navbat bilan ishlaymiz. Ro‘yxatni ko‘rmasdan sizning shaxsiy so‘zlaringizni bilaman deb aytmayman.',
 'Choose five useful words and record a meaning, natural combination and personal example. Recall them without looking tomorrow, then use them in new sentences after a few days. Share your list for meaning, gap-fill and sentence-production practice; I cannot see an unspecified personal list.')
add('spelling-varieties','base:393,637',
 'Britancha va amerikancha shakllarning ikkalasi ham kontekstga mos bo‘lsa ishlatiladi; bitta matnda izchillikni saqlang. Uch misol: colour — color; centre — center; organise — organize. Talaffuz farqi faqat yozilish bilan cheklanmaydi; bir xil so‘zni ishonchli audio bilan solishtiring.',
 'British and American forms can both be appropriate; keep your choices consistent within a text. Examples: colour/color, centre/center and organise/organize. Pronunciation differences are not fully captured by spelling, so compare reliable recordings of the same word.')
add('present-comparison','base:403',
 'Present simple odat va umumiy holatni, present continuous esa davom etayotgan yoki vaqtinchalik ishni ko‘rsatadi. Uch juftlik: 1) I work at home. — Uyda ishlayman. / I am working at home today. — Bugun uyda ishlayapman. 2) She reads every evening. — U har oqshom o‘qiydi. / She is reading now. — U hozir o‘qiyapti. 3) They play on Sundays. — Ular yakshanba kunlari o‘ynaydi. / They are playing now. — Ular hozir o‘ynayapti. Endi o‘zingiz haqingizda odat va hozirgi ishni yozing.',
 'Present simple describes habits or general states; present continuous describes an ongoing or temporary action. Compare: I work at home / I am working at home today; She reads every evening / She is reading now; They play on Sundays / They are playing now. Write one habit and one current action about yourself.')
add('future-continuous','base:406',
 'Future continuous: will be + V-ing. Kelajakdagi ma’lum paytda davom etayotgan ishni tasvirlaydi. 1) At eight, I will be studying. — Soat sakkizda o‘qiyotgan bo‘laman. 2) This time tomorrow, we will be travelling. — Ertaga shu paytda safarda ketayotgan bo‘lamiz. 3) She will be working when you arrive. — Siz kelganingizda u ishlayotgan bo‘ladi. Oddiy reja va o‘sha paytda davom etayotgan jarayonni ajrating.',
 'Future continuous uses will be + -ing for an action in progress at a future time. Examples: At eight, I will be studying. This time tomorrow, we will be travelling. She will be working when you arrive. Distinguish the ongoing activity at that time from a simple future event.')
add('conditional-comparison','base:410',
 'First conditional real ehtimolli kelajak uchun: if + present, will + V. Second conditional faraziy yoki hozirgi haqiqatga zid holat uchun: if + past, would + V. 1) If it rains, I will stay home. — Yomg‘ir yog‘sa, uyda qolaman. 2) If I had a car, I would drive there. — Mashinam bo‘lsa edi, u yerga haydab borardim. 3) If I were you, I would ask. — O‘rningizda bo‘lsam, so‘rardim. Shaklni emas, vaziyatning qanchalik real ekanini ham tekshiring.',
 'The first conditional commonly uses if + present, will + verb for a real future possibility. The second uses if + past, would + verb for a hypothetical situation. Examples: If it rains, I will stay home. If I had a car, I would drive there. If I were you, I would ask. Consider the intended likelihood, not just the form.')
add('advanced-grammar','base:422,423,426,427,443,444,446',
 'Uch foydali tuzilma: 1) Never have I seen this before. — Buni ilgari hech ko‘rmaganman; inkor ifodadan keyin inversion. 2) It was Ali who called. — Aynan Ali qo‘ng‘iroq qildi; cleft gap diqqatni Aliga qaratadi. 3) She likes reading, writing and swimming. — U o‘qish, yozish va suzishni yoqtiradi; parallel shakl saqlangan. Qaysi tuzilmani nazarda tutganingizni yozing, uning savol/inkor shaklini alohida ko‘ramiz.',
 'Three useful structures: Never have I seen this before illustrates inversion after a negative expression. It was Ali who called is a cleft focusing on Ali. She likes reading, writing and swimming keeps a parallel pattern. Name the construction you want so we can study its questions, negatives and limits.')
add('grammar-practice','base:432,433,434,436,439,442,448,450 extra:28,29,50,59,65,68,74,75,79',
 'Bitta qoidani uch bosqichda mashq qilamiz: tushunish, xatoni topish, mustaqil gap yozish. Masalan: 1) She works here. — U shu yerda ishlaydi. 2) Does she work here? — U shu yerda ishlaydimi? 3) She does not work here. — U shu yerda ishlamaydi. Does kelganda work’ga yana -s qo‘shilmaydi. Endi «he / study English» bilan shu uch shaklni o‘zingiz tuzing.',
 'Use three stages: understand a rule, identify an error, then produce your own sentence. Compare She works here; Does she work here?; She does not work here. After does, work takes no extra -s. Now make the same three forms with he / study English.')
add('mock-schedule','base:453,454,468,488,495,496,497,501,502,503,504,505,506,516,517,518,519,520,521,522,523,524,525,526,527,528,545,546,547,581,582,583,584,585,586,587,590',
 'Jadval, qatnashuv, yozuv, topshiriq va support holatlari jonli hisob ma’lumotiga bog‘liq. Tegishli bo‘lim yoki bildirishnomada ko‘ringan sana va statusni tekshiring; men bu savoldan navbatdagi dars vaqtini yoki qatnashganingizni bilmayman. Shaxsiy havolani ommaga tarqatmang. Qaysi dars yoki murojaat haqida so‘rayotganingizni aniq yozing.',
 'Schedules, attendance, recordings, assignments and support status require current account information. Check the relevant section or notification for the date and status; this question alone does not establish a next class time or attendance. Do not publish private access links. Name the class or request concerned.',kind='clarify')
add('media-study','base:529,530,531,532,533,534,535,537,538,540,541,542,543,544,548,549,550',
 'Media mashqi uchun qisqa bo‘lak tanlang. Avval umumiy fikrni tinglab ayting; keyin ruxsatli transkript bilan noma’lum joyni solishtiring; oxirida uchta asosiy fikr va o‘zingizning bitta gapingizni yozing. Aniq epizodni tahlil qilish uchun uning nomini ayting. Transkript yoki video ochilmagan bo‘lsa, uning mazmunini ko‘rdim deb aytmayman.',
 'Choose a short media segment. First listen for its main point, then compare unclear parts with an available transcript. Finish with three key points and one sentence of your own. Name the episode for specific analysis; I cannot claim to have seen content that was not available.')
add('identity','extra:1,2,3,4,5,7,10,11,12,17,18,19,20,100,101,102,106,109,118 base:556',
 'Men RIWI — Learners Area’dagi matnli o‘quv yordamchisiman 🙂 Odam ham, katta LLM agent ham emasman; ichki qoidalar va mavjud bilimlar bilan ishlayman. Ism yoki boshqa shaxsiy ma’lumot aytmasdan savol berishingiz mumkin. Atamaning ma’nosi, grammatika, mashq yoki sayt bo‘yicha bitta savoldan boshlaymiz. RIWI nomining tasdiqlanmagan kengaytmasini o‘ylab topmayman.',
 'I am RIWI, the text learning assistant in Learners Area. I am not a person or a large LLM agent; I use internal rules and available knowledge. You can ask without sharing your name. Start with a word, grammar point, practice task or site question. I will not invent an expansion of the name RIWI.')
add('honest-limits','base:557,558,596,957,958,959,962,963,964,989 extra:22,33,34,35,104,105,108,110,113,116',
 'Bilimim va qoidalarim cheklangan. Mos, tekshirilgan javob bo‘lmasa, bilmayman deyman yoki kerakli kontekstni so‘rayman. Men doimiy jonli internet qidiruvi, eng so‘nggi narx yoki yangilikni tekshirish imkoniga ega emasman. Muhim ma’lumotni tegishli rasmiy joyda qayta tekshiring; taxminni tasdiqlangan fakt qilib ko‘rsatmayman.',
 'My knowledge and rules are limited. Without a reliable match, I say so or ask for context. I do not have continuous live web search or verified current prices and news. Check important information with the appropriate official service; I will not present a guess as a verified fact.')
add('privacy-retention','base:561,569,570,571,572,574,597,965',
 'Shu faol suhbatdagi ruxsat etilgan kontekst keyingi savolni tushunishga yordam beradi. «/clear» yoki «/new chat» keyingi suhbat uchun bu kontekstni uzadi; bu buyruqlar serverdagi barcha yozuvlar butunlay o‘chirildi degani emas. Suhbatlar amaldagi saqlash muddatiga bo‘ysunadi. Xabarni avtomatik ravishda hamma uchun ishonchli bilim deb qabul qilmayman.',
 'Permitted context in the current conversation can help with follow-ups. /clear and /new chat reset the context used for future turns; they do not claim to permanently erase every server record. Conversations follow retention rules. A chat statement is not automatically accepted as shared knowledge.')
add('question-style','base:562,563,564,565,573,600,951,952,953,954,955,956,960,961,974,975,985,986,987,990,991,993,994,995,996,997,998,999,1000 extra:13,15,62,63,64,66,67,69,70,71,72,76,77,121-140,141,143,144,146-150,153,155,156,158,160,309,312,314,316,318,319,320',
 'Savolni mavzu + qiyin joy + misol shaklida yozing 🙂 Masalan: «Present perfect’da have nega kerak? I have finished degan gapni tushuntir». Davomiy savolda faol suhbatdagi mavzuni ishlataman; bir nechta ma’no bo‘lsa, qaysi birini nazarda tutganingizni so‘rayman. Aniq matn yoki variant bo‘lmasa, ko‘rdim yoki solishtirdim deb aytmayman.',
 'Try topic + difficult point + example, such as Why does present perfect need have in I have finished? Follow-ups can use the current conversation; I ask when the reference is ambiguous. Without the actual text or options, I cannot claim to have reviewed or compared them.',kind='clarify')
add('greeting','extra:81,82,83,85,86,87,88,91,99',
 'Salom! Shu yerdaman 🙂 Bugun bitta qiyin joyni birga aniqlab olamiz. Inglizcha gap, tushunmagan qoida yoki sayt bo‘yicha savolingizni yozing.',
 'Hi, I’m here 🙂 Share an English sentence, a confusing rule or a site question, and we can work through one difficulty together.')
add('thanks-bye','extra:92,93,94,95,96,97,98',
 'Arzimaydi 🙂 Bugungi o‘rganganingizdan bitta qoidani eslab, bitta yangi gapda ishlating. Keyin davom ettirishga tayyor bo‘lsangiz, shu mavzuni yoki yangi savolni yozing.',
 'You’re welcome 🙂 Recall one rule from today and use it in a new sentence. When you return, name that topic or ask a new question.')

language('actually','base:601','Actually — «aslida», «to‘g‘risini aytganda». U ko‘pincha oldingi taxminni tuzatadi; «hozir» degani emas.',
 'Actually often corrects an assumption or adds a surprising fact. It does not mean currently.',[
 ('Actually, I live in Namangan.','Aslida, men Namanganda yashayman.'),('I thought it was easy, but it was actually difficult.','Oson deb o‘ylagandim, ammo aslida qiyin ekan.'),('Actually, we have already met.','Aslida, biz allaqachon tanishganmiz.')])
language('eventually','base:602','Eventually — vaqt yoki qiyinchilikdan keyin «oxir-oqibat». Finally — kutish tugaganini, oxirgi bosqichni yoki ro‘yxatdagi yakuniy fikrni bildirishi mumkin.',
 'Eventually means in the end after some time or difficulty. Finally can express relief, the last step or the final point in a sequence.',[
 ('We eventually found the address.','Oxir-oqibat manzilni topdik.'),('The bus finally arrived!','Avtobus nihoyat keldi!'),('Finally, check your spelling.','Oxirida imloni tekshiring.')])
language('although-despite','base:603','Although’dan keyin ega + fe’l keladi. Despite’dan keyin ot yoki V-ing keladi; despite of emas. Despite the fact that’dan keyin esa to‘liq gap mumkin.',
 'Although introduces a clause. Despite takes a noun or -ing form, without of. Despite the fact that can introduce a full clause.',[
 ('Although it rained, we played.','Yomg‘ir yog‘sa ham o‘ynadik.'),('Despite the rain, we played.','Yomg‘irga qaramay o‘ynadik.'),('Despite feeling tired, she continued.','Charchaganiga qaramay u davom etdi.')])
language('used-to','base:604','Used to + V — ilgari bo‘lgan, hozir esa o‘zgargan odat yoki holat. Be used to + ot/V-ing esa «ko‘nikkan» degani; ular bir xil emas.',
 'Used to + base verb describes a former habit or state that has changed. Be used to + noun/-ing means be accustomed to something.',[
 ('I used to walk to school.','Ilgari maktabga piyoda borardim.'),('She used to live here.','U ilgari shu yerda yashardi.'),('I am used to getting up early.','Erta turishga ko‘nikkanman.')])
language('would-rather','base:605','Would rather + oddiy fe’l — «...ni afzal ko‘rardim». Bir kishining tanlovi uchun to qo‘shilmaydi. Boshqa odamning ishini xohlasangiz, ko‘pincha would rather + ega + past shakl ishlatiladi.',
 'Would rather + base verb expresses preference. It takes no to for the same subject. For another person’s action, would rather + subject + past form is common.',[
 ('I would rather stay home.','Uyda qolishni afzal ko‘rardim.'),('She would rather walk than drive.','U mashina haydashdan ko‘ra piyoda yurishni afzal ko‘radi.'),('I would rather you came tomorrow.','Ertaga kelganingizni ma’qul ko‘rardim.')])
language('as-long-as','base:606','As long as shart ma’nosida «...bo‘lsa», «...sharti bilan» degani. Kelajak shartida undan keyin odatda present simple ishlatiladi. Boshqa vaziyatda davomiylikni ham bildirishi mumkin.',
 'As long as can mean provided that. In a future condition, it usually takes a present form. In other contexts it can describe duration.',[
 ('You can borrow it as long as you return it.','Qaytarsangiz, uni olib turishingiz mumkin.'),('We will go as long as the weather is fine.','Havo yaxshi bo‘lsa boramiz.'),('Stay as long as you need.','Qancha kerak bo‘lsa, shuncha qoling.')])
language('interested','base:608','Interested in odatda mavzu yoki faoliyatga qiziqishni bildiradi: ot/V-ing. Interested to hear/learn esa biror yangilikni bilishga qiziqishni yoki unga munosabatni ifodalaydi. Har fe’l bilan to ishlatib bo‘lmaydi.',
 'Interested in commonly introduces a topic or activity with a noun/-ing form. Interested to hear/learn expresses interest in learning information; to is not freely interchangeable with in.',[
 ('I am interested in history.','Tarixga qiziqaman.'),('She is interested in learning English.','U ingliz tilini o‘rganishga qiziqadi.'),('I would be interested to hear your view.','Fikringizni eshitish menga qiziq bo‘lardi.')])
language('borrow-lend','base:614','Borrow — boshqa kishidan vaqtincha olish. Lend — boshqaga vaqtincha berish. Yo‘nalishni tekshiring: borrow from, lend to.',
 'Borrow means receive something temporarily; lend means give it temporarily. Check the direction: borrow from, lend to.',[
 ('Can I borrow your pen?','Ruchkangizni olib tursam bo‘ladimi?'),('I lent my book to Ali.','Kitobimni Aliga berib turdim.'),('She borrowed a bike from me.','U mendan velosiped olib turdi.')])
language('say-tell','base:615','Say — aytilgan gap; tell — odatda kimga aytilgani ham keladi. Speak — til yoki rasmiyroq gapirish, talk — suhbatlashish. Tell me, say to me; say me emas.',
 'Say focuses on words; tell commonly takes a person. Speak is used for languages and some formal contexts; talk often means converse. Use tell me or say to me, not say me.',[
 ('She said hello.','U salom dedi.'),('Tell me the story.','Menga voqeani aytib bering.'),('We talked about school, and he spoke English.','Maktab haqida suhbatlashdik, u inglizcha gapirdi.')])
language('job-work','base:616','Job — sanaladigan ish o‘rni yoki alohida vazifa. Work ish faoliyati ma’nosida odatda sanalmaydi; a work bu ma’noda ishlatilmaydi.',
 'Job is countable: a position or task. Work is usually uncountable when it means employment or activity.',[
 ('She has a new job.','Uning yangi ishi bor.'),('I have a lot of work today.','Bugun ishim ko‘p.'),('Painting the door is a small job.','Eshikni bo‘yash — kichik bir vazifa.')])
language('fun-funny','base:617','Fun — maroqli, zavqli. Funny — kulgili yoki kontekstga qarab g‘alati. A fun lesson qiziqarli dars; a funny joke kulgili hazil.',
 'Fun means enjoyable. Funny means amusing or sometimes strange. A fun activity need not make you laugh.',[
 ('The game was fun.','O‘yin maroqli bo‘ldi.'),('That joke was funny.','U hazil kulgili edi.'),('The engine makes a funny noise.','Motor g‘alati ovoz chiqaryapti.')])
language('meet-know','base:618','Meet — uchrashish yoki ilk tanishish. Get to know — vaqt davomida yaxshiroq tanib borish. Know — tanish/bilish holati.',
 'Meet can describe an encounter or first introduction. Get to know is the process of becoming familiar; know is the resulting state.',[
 ('I met her yesterday.','U bilan kecha tanishdim yoki uchrashdim; kontekst muhim.'),('We got to know each other at school.','Maktabda bir-birimizni yaxshiroq tanidik.'),('I know him well.','Uni yaxshi taniyman.')])
language('late','base:621,629','«Men bugun kech qoldim» — I was late today. Uzrda nimaga kechikkaningizni aniqlashtirish mumkin; excuse me e’tibor so‘rashda ham ishlatiladi.',
 'I was late today describes arriving late. For an apology, say what happened briefly and take responsibility.',[
 ('I was late today.','Bugun kech qoldim.'),('I’m sorry I’m late.','Kechikkanim uchun uzr.'),('Sorry for keeping you waiting.','Sizni kuttirib qo‘yganim uchun uzr.')])
language('if-time','base:622','«Vaqtim bo‘lsa, yordam beraman» — If I have time, I will help. Kelajakdagi real shartni if ichida present simple, asosiy gapda will bilan ifodalash mumkin.',
 'If I have time, I will help expresses a real future condition. The if clause uses a present form, not will have in this ordinary pattern.',[
 ('If I have time, I will help.','Vaqtim bo‘lsa, yordam beraman.'),('If she calls, I will answer.','U qo‘ng‘iroq qilsa, javob beraman.'),('If we finish early, we will walk home.','Erta tugatsak, uyga piyoda qaytamiz.')])
language('seen-before','base:623','«Men buni oldin ham ko‘rganman» — I have seen this before. Aniq tugagan vaqt aytilmasa, oldingi tajriba hozir bilan bog‘lanadi. Yesterday kabi tugagan vaqt bilan odatda past simple tanlanadi.',
 'I have seen this before describes prior experience connected to now. With a finished time such as yesterday, use past simple for the event.',[
 ('I have seen this before.','Buni ilgari ko‘rganman.'),('She has visited Bukhara twice.','U Buxoroga ikki marta borgan.'),('I saw it yesterday.','Uni kecha ko‘rdim.')])
language('ice','base:625','Break the ice — noqulay yoki yangi suhbatni erkinlashtirish, odamlarni gapga kirishtirish. Bu ibora har doim muz sindirish haqida emas.',
 'Break the ice means make a new or awkward social situation more relaxed.',[
 ('A simple question helped break the ice.','Oddiy savol suhbatni erkin boshlashga yordam berdi.'),('We played a game to break the ice.','Tanishib, erkinlashish uchun o‘yin o‘ynadik.'),('Her joke broke the ice.','Uning hazili noqulaylikni yo‘qotdi.')])
language('blue-moon','base:626','Once in a blue moon — «juda kamdan-kam». Aniq oy sanasini hisoblash emas, odatning kamligini ifodalovchi ibora.',
 'Once in a blue moon means very rarely, not a precise calendar interval.',[
 ('I eat fast food once in a blue moon.','Tez tayyor ovqatni juda kam yeyman.'),('He visits us once in a blue moon.','U biznikiga kamdan-kam keladi.'),('We see snow here once in a blue moon.','Bu yerda qorni juda kam ko‘ramiz.')])
language('cup-tea','base:627','Not my cup of tea — didimga mos emas, unchalik yoqtirmayman. Bu muloyim shaxsiy afzallik ifodasi; narsani hamma uchun yomon demaydi.',
 'Not my cup of tea means not something I particularly enjoy. It expresses personal preference rather than a universal criticism.',[
 ('Horror films are not my cup of tea.','Qo‘rqinchli filmlar didimga mos emas.'),('Camping is not really my cup of tea.','Chodirda dam olishni uncha yoqtirmayman.'),('It’s a good game, but not my cup of tea.','Yaxshi o‘yin, lekin mening didimga mos emas.')])
language('happy','base:628','Happy, pleased va glad vaziyatga qarab xursandlikni bildiradi. Happy with — natijadan mamnun; glad to hear — yangilikni eshitib xursand.',
 'Happy, pleased and glad express related feelings with different common patterns.',[
 ('I’m happy with the result.','Natijadan mamnunman.'),('I’m glad to hear that.','Buni eshitganimdan xursandman.'),('She was pleased to see us.','U bizni ko‘rib xursand bo‘ldi.')])
language('shop','base:630 extra:256','Narx so‘rashda sodda, muloyim savol yetarli. Suhbatni boshlaymiz: Shop assistant: Hello! How can I help you? Siz xaridor sifatida javob yozishingiz mumkin.',
 'Use a simple polite question when shopping. Role-play: Shop assistant: Hello! How can I help you? Reply as the customer.',[
 ('How much is this?','Bu qancha turadi?'),('Do you have it in a smaller size?','Buning kichikroq o‘lchami bormi?'),('Could I pay by card?','Karta bilan to‘lasam bo‘ladimi?')])
language('restaurant','base:631','Qisqa suhbat: Waiter: Are you ready to order? Customer: Yes, please. Could I have the vegetable soup? Waiter: Certainly. Anything to drink? Customer: Water, please.',
 'Mini-dialogue: Waiter: Are you ready to order? Customer: Yes, please. Could I have the vegetable soup? Waiter: Certainly. Anything to drink? Customer: Water, please.',[
 ('Could I see the menu, please?','Menyuni ko‘rsam bo‘ladimi?'),('Does this contain nuts?','Bunda yong‘oq bormi?'),('Could we have the bill, please?','Hisobni bersangiz.')])
language('hotel','base:632','Qisqa suhbat: Guest: I’d like to book a room for two nights. Receptionist: For how many people? Guest: Two adults. Receptionist: Which dates? Guest: From Friday to Sunday. Bu mashq; haqiqiy bron bajarilmadi.',
 'Mini-dialogue: Guest: I’d like to book a room for two nights. Receptionist: For how many people? Guest: Two adults. Receptionist: Which dates? Guest: From Friday to Sunday. This is language practice, not a real reservation.',[
 ('Do you have a room available?','Bo‘sh xonangiz bormi?'),('Is breakfast included?','Nonushta narxga kiradimi?'),('What time is check-out?','Xonani soat nechada topshirish kerak?')])
language('airport','base:633,643','Aeroportda xodimdan qisqa va aniq so‘rang. Mashq: Staff member: Hello. Where are you travelling today? Siz yo‘lovchi sifatida javob yozing; men haqiqiy reys yoki darvozani tekshirmayapman.',
 'Ask staff a short, clear question. Role-play: Staff member: Hello. Where are you travelling today? Reply as the passenger. I am not checking real flight or gate information.',[
 ('Where is the check-in desk?','Ro‘yxatdan o‘tish joyi qayerda?'),('How do I get to gate twelve?','O‘n ikkinchi chiqish darvozasiga qanday boraman?'),('Could you help me find the baggage claim?','Yuk olish joyini topishga yordam bera olasizmi?')])
language('introduction','base:634 extra:306,307','Tanishtiruvni hozirgi faoliyat + tegishli tajriba + maqsad bilan tuzing. Tajribani o‘ylab topmang. O‘zingizga mos ma’lumot bilan quyidagi namunani o‘zgartiring.',
 'Structure an introduction as current activity, relevant experience and goal. Replace the sample with truthful personal details.',[
 ('I’m a student interested in software development.','Dastur yaratishga qiziqadigan talabaman.'),('I built a small website as a practice project.','Mashq loyihasi sifatida kichik sayt yaratdim.'),('I’d like to improve my skills by working with a team.','Jamoada ishlab ko‘nikmalarimni oshirmoqchiman.')])
language('email','base:635 extra:305,315','Rasmiy xatda murojaat, maqsad va so‘rov aniq bo‘ladi. Do‘stona xatda ohang erkinroq, lekin maqsad baribir tushunarli bo‘lsin. Ism yoki vaziyatni o‘ylab topmay, andazadagi joyni o‘zingiz to‘ldiring.',
 'A formal email needs an appropriate greeting, clear purpose and polite request. Friendly emails can be more relaxed. Replace placeholders with real details.',[
 ('Dear Ms Karimova, I am writing to ask about the course.','Hurmatli Karimova xonim, kurs haqida so‘ramoqchiman.'),('Could you let me know when the lesson starts?','Dars qachon boshlanishini ayta olasizmi?'),('Hi Ali, thanks for your message!','Salom Ali, xabaring uchun rahmat!')])
language('informal-contractions','base:636','Gonna va wanna norasmiy nutqdagi qisqargan shakllar; rasmiy yozuvda going to va want to ishlating. Gonna asosan reja/kelajakdagi going to + fe’l o‘rnida; har qanday going to’ni almashtirmaydi.',
 'Gonna and wanna represent informal speech forms. Use going to and want to in formal writing. Gonna does not replace every occurrence of going to, especially a destination phrase.',[
 ('I’m going to study tonight.','Bugun kechqurun o‘qimoqchiman.'),('I want to ask a question.','Savol bermoqchiman.'),('I’m going to school.','Maktabga ketyapman; bu joyga borish ma’nosi.')])
language('small-talk','base:642,644','Yengil suhbatda savol + javobga qiziqish + o‘zingizdan qisqa fikr ishlating. Muloyim rozi bo‘lmaslikda odamni emas, fikrni muhokama qiling.',
 'For small talk, ask, respond with interest and add a brief detail. In disagreement, address the idea rather than attacking the person.',[
 ('How has your week been?','Haftangiz qanday o‘tyapti?'),('That sounds interesting. How did you start?','Qiziq ekan. Qanday boshlagansiz?'),('I see your point, but I have a different view.','Fikringizni tushundim, ammo boshqacha qarashim bor.')])
add('translation-input','base:648,649',
 'Tarjima qilish kerak bo‘lgan maqol yoki matnning o‘zini yuboring. Ma’no, ohang va vaziyatni saqlashga harakat qilamiz; aynan mos maqol bo‘lmasa, mazmuniy tarjimani alohida aytaman. Matn berilmaganida uning tarjimasini o‘ylab topmayman.',
 'Share the actual proverb or text. We can preserve meaning, tone and context; if there is no exact equivalent, I will distinguish a meaning-based translation. I cannot translate text that was not supplied.',kind='clarify')
add('ten-questions','base:650',
 'Mana kundalik mashq uchun o‘nta savol 🙂\n1) What time do you get up?\n2) How do you get to school or work?\n3) What do you usually have for breakfast?\n4) What are you studying now?\n5) What did you do yesterday?\n6) What do you enjoy doing?\n7) Who do you spend time with?\n8) What would you like to learn?\n9) What are your plans for tomorrow?\n10) Why is that important to you?\nBirinchi savolga ikki-uch gap bilan javob bering.',
 'Ten everyday practice questions: 1) What time do you get up? 2) How do you get to school or work? 3) What do you usually have for breakfast? 4) What are you studying now? 5) What did you do yesterday? 6) What do you enjoy doing? 7) Who do you spend time with? 8) What would you like to learn? 9) What are your plans for tomorrow? 10) Why is that important to you? Start with two or three sentences answering the first.')

add('small-habit','base:50,651,652,660,661,671,672,674,677,678,681,682,691,692,695,696,700,799,800,851,853,854,855,856,857,881,882,883,884,885,886,899,900,988 extra:301,302,303,304,310',
 'Rejani kichik va tekshiriladigan qiling: bugun bitta muhim ishni tanlang, boshlash vaqtini yozing va 10–15 daqiqalik birinchi qadam belgilang. Masalan, «inglizchani yaxshilayman» o‘rniga «soat 19:00 da beshta so‘zni yopiq holda eslab, uchta gap yozaman». Oxirida nima bajarildi va qaysi to‘siq bo‘lganini qayd eting; ertangi hajmni shunga moslang. Qat’iy bitta jadval hammaga mos emas.',
 'Make the plan small and observable: choose one priority, schedule a start time and define a ten-to-fifteen-minute first step. Replace improve my English with recall five words and write three sentences at 19:00. Record what you completed and what blocked you, then adjust tomorrow. No single schedule suits everyone.')
add('pomodoro','base:653,662',
 'Bir vazifaga qisqa vaqt ajrating: masalan, 25 daqiqa ishlash va 5 daqiqa tanaffus. Shu orada bildirishnomalarni chetga qo‘yib, faqat bitta aniq ishni bajaring. Bu majburiy 25/5 qonuni emas; diqqat va vazifaga qarab qisqartiring. Taymer tugaganda bajarganingizni tekshiring, faqat vaqt o‘tganini emas.',
 'Try a focused block, such as twenty-five minutes of work followed by a five-minute break. Silence distractions and define one task. The 25/5 pattern is an adjustable technique, not a universal rule. Check what you produced, not just how much time elapsed.')
add('explain-back','base:656,666,667,668,688,689',
 'Mavzuni o‘qib bo‘lgach, kitobni yopib o‘z so‘zingiz bilan tushuntiring. Tushuntirishdagi bo‘sh joyni topib, aynan shu qismini tekshiring. Konspektda chapga savollar, o‘ngga qisqa dalil va misollar, pastga xulosa yozish mumkin. Bir nechta materialni yig‘ishdan ko‘ra bitta qoidani yangi vaziyatda ishlata olishni sinang.',
 'After studying, close the material and explain it in your own words. Identify a gap, check that part and explain again. Notes can put questions on the left, evidence/examples on the right and a summary below. Test application in a new situation rather than merely collecting sources.')
add('two-languages','base:658',
 'Ikki tilni parallel o‘rganish mumkin, lekin har biriga alohida vaqt va aniq maqsad bering. Bir xil yangi so‘zlarni chalkashtirsangiz, mashq kunlari yoki kontekstlarini ajrating. Bir haftadan keyin har ikkala tilda mustaqil nima qila olganingizni tekshirib, vaqtni qayta taqsimlang.',
 'You can study two languages alongside each other, with separate time blocks and goals. If new items become confused, separate practice days or contexts. Review what you can independently do in each language after a week and adjust the balance.')
add('exam-preparation','base:664,665,673,680,684,685,686,687,697,698,973',
 'Avval imtihon talabi va o‘zingiz xato qilayotgan vazifa turini aniqlang. Bitta kichik mashqni vaqt bilan bajaring, xatoni «bilim», «savolni tushunish», «vaqt» yoki «format» deb belgilang, keyin shu sababga mos mashq qiling. Oxirgi kunlarda faqat yangi mavzu yig‘mang: xatolarni takrorlang va jihoz/jadvalni tekshiring. Bitta past natija butun qobiliyatingizni belgilamaydi.',
 'Identify the test requirements and the task causing trouble. Do a short timed practice, classify errors as knowledge, understanding, time or format, then target the cause. Near the test, review recurring errors and check logistics rather than only adding new topics. One low result does not define your overall ability.')
add('music','base:675',
 'Musiqaning ta’siri odam va vazifaga bog‘liq. Ayniqsa matn o‘qishda so‘zli musiqa chalg‘itishi mumkin. Bir xil murakkablikdagi ikki qisqa vazifani jimlikda va musiqa bilan bajarib, tezlik hamda xatoni solishtiring; faqat yoqqaniga qarab hukm qilmang.',
 'The effect depends on the person and task; lyrics can compete with verbal work. Compare two similar short tasks in quiet and with music, checking both time and errors rather than preference alone.')
add('rest','base:663,852,858,859,860,861,862,863,864,865,866,867,868,869,870,871',
 'Charchoqni darrov «dangasalik» deb baholamang. Qisqa tanaffus, muntazam uyqu va o‘zingizga mos yengil harakat o‘qish tartibini qo‘llab-quvvatlaydi. Ovqatlanish yoki mashq bo‘yicha shaxsiy tashxis va qat’iy me’yor bera olmayman; ehtiyoj yosh, sog‘liq va sharoitga bog‘liq. Kuchli yoki davomli alomat bo‘lsa malakali tibbiy yordamga murojaat qiling.',
 'Do not label fatigue as laziness. Short breaks, regular sleep and suitable light activity can support a study routine. I cannot diagnose symptoms or prescribe an individual diet, exercise dose or fluid target; needs vary by health, age and circumstances. Persistent or severe symptoms need qualified medical advice.')
add('communication','base:763,764,792,872,873,874,875,876,877,878,879,880,939,940',
 'Avval vaziyatni bahosiz ayting, keyin ta’siri va aniq iltimosni yozing. Masalan: «Vazifa o‘zgarganini kech bildim, vaqtim yetmadi. Keyingi safar oldinroq ayta olasizmi?» Qarshi tomonni tinglang va tushunganingizni qisqa qaytaring. Rad etishda «Hozir bunga ulgurmayman, lekin ertaga ko‘rib chiqaman» kabi aniq chegara qo‘ying.',
 'Describe what happened without insults, explain the impact and make a concrete request. For example: I learned about the change late and could not finish; could you tell me earlier next time? Listen and briefly confirm what you understood. A polite refusal can set a clear limit and offer a realistic alternative.')
add('shopping-plan','base:887,888,889,890 extra:308',
 'Avval mavjud narsalarni tekshiring. Ro‘yxatni zarur, keyinga qolishi mumkin va ixtiyoriy qismlarga ajrating; miqdor va budjet yozing. Ovqat rejasi uchun bir xil mahsulotdan bir nechta sodda taom rejalash mumkin. Shaxsiy ro‘yxatingizni yuborsangiz, undagi narsalarni tartiblaymiz; ko‘rmagan ro‘yxatni allaqachon saraladim demayman.',
 'Check what you already have, then separate essentials, deferrable items and optional purchases, with quantities and a budget. Shared ingredients can simplify meal planning. Share your actual list for sorting; I cannot claim to have organised an unseen one.')
add('recipe-ratio','base:891',
 'Yangi porsiya sonini eski porsiya soniga bo‘ling va har ingredient miqdorini shu koeffitsiyentga ko‘paytiring. Masalan, ikki kishilik retseptni to‘rt kishiga: 4÷2=2; 200 g guruch → 400 g. Pishirish vaqti ham aynan ikki baravar bo‘ladi deb taxmin qilmang; idish va tayyorlikni tekshirish kerak.',
 'Divide the new serving count by the original, then multiply ingredient quantities by that factor. For two servings changed to four, the factor is 2: 200 g rice becomes 400 g. Cooking time does not automatically double; check the vessel and doneness.')
add('travel-checklist','base:892,893,923,924,947,950 extra:311',
 'Safar uchun manzil, sana, yo‘l va qaytish variantini, budjetni, hujjat talablarini va bog‘lanish rejasini tekshiring. Ish vaqti, chipta narxi, ob-havo va kirish qoidalari o‘zgaradi; ularni ketishdan oldin rasmiy xizmatdan tekshiring. Qaysi shahar, necha kun va qanday cheklov borligini yozsangiz, taxminlarni belgilagan holda reja tuzamiz.',
 'Check destination, dates, outbound/return transport, budget, documents and a contact plan. Opening times, fares, weather and entry requirements change, so verify them with the relevant official service before travelling. Share the city, duration and constraints for a plan with explicit assumptions.')
add('digital-security','base:726,747,748,894,895,976,977,978,979,980,981',
 'Shubhali havolani ochishdan oldin domen va jo‘natuvchini mustaqil tekshiring. Shoshiltirish, pul yoki tasdiqlash kodi so‘rash xavf belgisi. Kod, parol va tokenni yubormang; rasmiy ilova/saytni o‘zingiz oching. Men havolani xavfsizlik skanerida tekshirganimni ayta olmayman. Yo‘qolgan qurilma yoki begona kirishda rasmiy sessiya va tiklash boshqaruvidan foydalaning.',
 'Verify the domain and sender independently before following a suspicious link. Urgency, payment demands and requests for verification codes are warning signs. Do not share secrets; open the official app or site yourself. I have not scanned the link. Use official session and recovery controls for a lost device or suspected intrusion.')
add('home-tech','base:896,897,898',
 'Avval muammoni ajrating: bitta qurilmadami yoki hammasidami? Internetda boshqa sayt va qurilmani solishtiring; xotirada esa katta fayllar va saqlash ko‘rsatkichini tekshiring. O‘chirishdan oldin zarur fayl nusxasi borligiga ishonch hosil qiling. Elektr qurilmasini ochib ta’mirlash yoki himoya sozlamalarini o‘chirishni tavsiya qilmayman.',
 'Isolate whether the issue affects one device or all devices. Compare another site/device for connectivity, or inspect storage usage and large files for capacity. Preserve needed files before deleting anything. Do not open electrical equipment or disable security protections as a routine fix.')
add('teacher-plan','extra:261,263,265,266,267,268,269,270,271,272,273,274,275,276,278,279',
 'Umumiy dars rejasi: 5 daqiqa eski bilimni eslash; 8 daqiqa bitta tushuncha va model; 10 daqiqa yo‘naltirilgan mashq; 10 daqiqa juftlikda mustaqil qo‘llash; 5 daqiqa tekshirish va refleksiya. Uch daraja: tayanch iborali gap, tayanchsiz gap, yangi vaziyatda sababli javob. Feedback’da odamga baho emas, «shu gapda mana bu qoida» deb aniq dalil bering. Uy vazifasi: maqsad + topshiriladigan ish + muddat. Bu tavsiya, darsni tizimga yaratish yoki xabar yuborish amali emas.',
 'A general lesson plan: five minutes retrieval, eight modelling one concept, ten guided practice, ten independent pair work and five review/reflection. Differentiate with a supported sentence, an unsupported sentence and transfer to a new situation. Give evidence about the work rather than labels about the learner. Homework needs a goal, deliverable and deadline. This is a suggested plan, not a created lesson or sent message.')
add('teacher-quiz','extra:262',
 'B1 uchun kichik mashq 🙂\n1) She has lived here ___ 2020. (since/for)\n2) If it rains, we ___ stay home. (will/would)\n3) The letter ___ yesterday. (was sent/has sent)\nAvval o‘quvchi sababini tushuntirsin. O‘qituvchi kaliti: 1) since — boshlanish nuqtasi; 2) will — real kelajak sharti; 3) was sent — o‘tgan zamon majhul nisbat. Bular yangi, baholanmaydigan misollar.',
 'A short original practice quiz: 1) She has lived here ___ 2020 (since/for). 2) If it rains, we ___ stay home (will/would). 3) The letter ___ yesterday (was sent/has sent). Ask learners to justify their choices first. Teacher key: since for a starting point; will for a real future condition; was sent for past passive. These are new ungraded examples.')
add('admin-guidance','extra:281-285,287-293,295-300',
 'Ma’muriy ishda eng kam zarur ruxsatni saqlang: haqiqiy sessiya roli, amal vakolati, obyekt doirasi va auditni tekshiring. Teacher biriktirishda aynan qaysi guruh va muddat ekanini tasdiqlang. Akademik matn va ballarni operatsion ro‘yxatga qo‘shmang. Export yoki rol o‘zgartirish tegishli boshqaruv jarayonida bajariladi; chatdagi so‘rov uni bajardi degani emas. Siz aynan qaysi amal bo‘yicha yo‘riqnoma xohlaysiz?',
 'Use least privilege: verify the session role, permitted action, object scope and audit trail. Teacher assignments need an exact group and duration. Keep academic answers and scores out of operational lists. Exports and role changes belong to their authorised management workflow; a chat reply does not perform them. Which action needs guidance?')
add('live-chat','base:509,510,511,512',
 'Jonli dars sahifasidagi chatning ko‘rinish va ishtirok qoidalarini tekshiring. Umumiy chatni shaxsiy yozishma deb qabul qilmang: boshqalar ko‘rishi mumkin. Maxfiy ma’lumot kiritmang, savolni dars mavzusiga bog‘lab qisqa yozing. Men hozirgi dars chatini ko‘rganimni yoki xabar yuborganimni ayta olmayman.',
 'Check the live lesson’s chat visibility and participation rules. Treat a shared chat as visible to others rather than private. Leave out sensitive information and ask a brief question related to the lesson. I have not inspected the current chat or sent a message.')
add('own-report','base:589',
 'O‘z natijangiz bo‘yicha yordam uchun akkauntga kirgan bo‘lishingiz va aynan o‘zingizga tegishli ruxsatli urinish tanlangan bo‘lishi kerak. Natija yoki progress bo‘limini oching. Bu javobdan hali shaxsiy hisobot o‘qilgani kelib chiqmaydi; kerakli ma’lumot bo‘lmasa uni o‘ylab topmayman.',
 'Your results require a valid session and an authorised attempt belonging to you. Open the result or progress section. This reply does not mean a personal report has already been read; missing data will not be invented.',kind='conditional')

# Short definitions stay distinct; current vendor prices and guarantees are excluded.
TECH='''701|Maqsadga qarab tanlang: web sahifa uchun HTML/CSS va JavaScript; avtomatlashtirish uchun Python bilan kichik loyiha boshlash mumkin. Bir vaqtda ko‘p til emas, o‘zgaruvchi, shart, sikl, funksiya va xatoni tekshirishni o‘rganing.|Choose by goal: HTML/CSS and JavaScript for web pages, or Python for a small automation project. Focus on variables, conditions, loops, functions and debugging rather than collecting languages.
702|Python — o‘qilishi qulay sintaksisli, umumiy maqsadli til. Avtomatlashtirish, web va ma’lumot tahlilida ishlatiladi. Mashhurlikning o‘zi har loyiha uchun eng yaxshi tanlov degani emas.|Python is a general-purpose language with readable syntax, used for automation, web work and data analysis. Popularity does not make it the best choice for every project.
703|HTML hujjat tuzilishi va mazmunini belgilovchi markup tili. CSS uning ko‘rinishi va joylashuvini ifodalaydi. Ular JavaScript kabi umumiy maqsadli dasturlash tili bilan bir vazifani bajarmaydi.|HTML describes document structure and content; CSS describes presentation and layout. They serve different roles from a general-purpose programming language such as JavaScript.
704|JavaScript brauzerda tugma, forma va boshqa interaktiv harakatlarni boshqaradi; mos runtime bilan serverda ham ishlaydi. Misol: forma tekshirish, ma’lumot so‘rash va javobni sahifada chiqarish.|JavaScript controls interactive browser behaviour and can run on servers with a suitable runtime. Examples include validating a form, requesting data and updating the page.
705|Frontend — foydalanuvchi ko‘radigan interfeys. Backend — serverdagi qoidalar, ruxsat va ma’lumot bilan ishlash. Tugmani yashirish backend ruxsat tekshiruvining o‘rnini bosmaydi.|Frontend is the user-facing interface; backend handles server rules, permissions and data. Hiding a button is not a substitute for server authorisation.
706|API — dasturlar o‘rtasida kelishilgan so‘rov-javob chegarasi. Masalan, ob-havo ilovasi shahar kodi bilan so‘rov beradi, xizmat belgilangan shaklda javob qaytaradi. API ruxsatsiz hamma ma’lumotni ochadi degani emas.|An API is an agreed interface between programs. A weather app might request a city’s forecast and receive a structured response. An API does not imply unrestricted data access.
707|REST — resurslar va ularning holati atrofida tuziladigan arxitektura uslubi. HTTP API’da URL resursni, metod amalni, status esa natijani bildirishi mumkin. Har JSON endpoint avtomatik to‘liq REST bo‘lavermaydi.|REST is an architectural style organised around resources and representations. In an HTTP API, a URL may identify a resource, a method the action, and a status the result. JSON alone does not make an API RESTful.
708|GET resurs ko‘rinishini olish uchun; uning semantikasi server holatini o‘zgartirmasligi kerak. POST resursga ma’lumotni qayta ishlash uchun yuboradi. GET manzilidagi parametrga sir yozmang; POST ham o‘z-o‘zidan shifrlash emas.|GET retrieves a representation and is intended to be safe. POST submits data for processing. Do not place secrets in URLs; POST itself is not encryption.
709|404 — so‘ralgan resurs topilmadi. 500 — server so‘rovni bajarishda kutilmagan xatoga uchradi. Status sababni to‘liq ko‘rsatmaydi: vaqt, request ID va xavfsiz diagnostika kerak.|404 means the requested resource was not found; 500 means an unexpected server error prevented fulfilment. The status alone does not establish the root cause; use safe diagnostics and a request ID.
710|FastAPI — Python’da API yaratish frameworki. Tur annotatsiyalari bilan kirish ma’lumotini tekshirish va API sxemasini yaratishga yordam beradi. Baribir autentifikatsiya, ruxsat va testlarni o‘zingiz to‘g‘ri loyihalashingiz kerak.|FastAPI is a Python framework for building APIs, using type annotations for validation and API schemas. Authentication, authorisation and tests still need sound design.
711|Django yaxlit web ilova uchun ORM va admin kabi ko‘p tayyor qismlarni beradi. FastAPI ko‘proq API markazli ishga mos tuzilma beradi. Tanlov mavjud loyiha, jamoa, ma’lumot modeli va operatsion talabga bog‘liq.|Django offers an integrated web framework with components such as an ORM and admin interface. FastAPI centres on APIs. Choose according to the existing stack, team, data model and operational needs.
712|Database ma’lumotni tizimli saqlash, topish va mos ravishda yangilash uchun kerak. Masalan, foydalanuvchi, kurs va urinish alohida yozuvlar bo‘ladi. Ularning bog‘lanishi va ruxsatlari ham loyihalanadi.|A database stores, retrieves and updates structured records, such as users, courses and attempts. Relationships and access rules are part of the design.
713|SQL — so‘rov tili; odatda relational jadvallar bilan ishlatiladi. NoSQL esa hujjat, key-value yoki boshqa modellar oilasiga aytiladi. Ular «biri tez, biri sekin» degan oddiy qoida bilan ajralmaydi.|SQL is a query language commonly used with relational tables. NoSQL covers families such as document and key-value databases. The distinction is not simply fast versus slow.
714|PostgreSQL — ochiq kodli relational ma’lumotlar bazasi. Tranzaksiya, cheklovlar va indekslar orqali ma’lumot yaxlitligi hamda so‘rovlarni boshqaradi. Indeks qo‘shishdan oldin haqiqiy so‘rov va rejasini o‘lchang.|PostgreSQL is an open-source relational database with transactions, constraints and indexes. Measure the real query and plan before assuming an extra index will help.
715|Supabase boshqariladigan PostgreSQL asosida auth, storage va boshqa integratsiya qismlarini beradi. Mijoz interfeysi borligi ma’lumot xavfsizligini o‘zidan-o‘zi ta’minlamaydi; server ruxsatlari va RLS to‘g‘ri sozlanishi kerak. Joriy tarifni jonli tekshirmayman.|Supabase provides managed PostgreSQL with related auth, storage and integration features. Client access does not itself ensure security; authorisation and RLS must be configured correctly. I am not verifying current plans or prices.
716|Git fayl o‘zgarishlari tarixini yuritadi. GitHub esa repositoryni saqlash va hamkorlik qilish xizmatidir. Commit tarixni qayd etadi; remote’ga push qilish alohida amal.|Git tracks file history. GitHub hosts repositories and collaboration tools. A commit records a change; pushing it to a remote is a separate action.
717|Commit — tarixdagi saqlangan o‘zgarish nuqtasi. Branch — commitlar zanjiriga ko‘chib boradigan nomli ko‘rsatkich. Branch yangi loyiha nusxasi degani emas.|A commit records a revision. A branch is a named movable pointer to a line of commits, not necessarily an independent copy of the project.
718|Merge conflict o‘zgarishlarni Git avtomatik birlashtira olmaganda chiqadi. Ikkala tomon maqsadini ko‘rib, yakuniy kodni tuzating va tegishli testni bajaring. Shunchaki bir tomonni tanlash ishlayotgan xulqni yo‘qotishi mumkin.|A merge conflict occurs when Git cannot combine changes automatically. Understand both intentions, resolve the result and run relevant tests. Blindly taking one side can discard working behaviour.
719|Pull request o‘zgarishni ko‘rib chiqish, test dalili va muhokama uchun chegaradir. Reviewer muammo, natijadagi xulq va xavfni tushunishi kerak. PR ochilgani merge yoki production deploy bajarildi degani emas.|A pull request provides a review boundary for changes, tests and discussion. Reviewers need the problem, resulting behaviour and risks. An open PR does not mean merge or production deployment occurred.
720|CI o‘zgarishlarni avtomatik yig‘ish va tekshirishga yordam beradi. CD yetkazib berish/deploy jarayonini avtomatlashtirishi mumkin. Yashil tekshiruv barcha qurilma va production holati tekshirildi degani emas.|CI automates integration checks and builds. CD can automate delivery or deployment. Passing CI does not establish every device or production acceptance condition.
721|Hosting xizmatlarini nomi bilan emas, ilovaning runtime, doimiy jarayon, ma’lumotlar bazasi, hudud va xarajat talabi bilan solishtiring. Joriy limit va narxlarni ularning rasmiy hujjatidan tekshirish kerak; men hozir ularni tekshirmayapman.|Compare hosting platforms by runtime, long-running processes, data needs, regions and cost rather than brand alone. Current limits and prices require official verification; I am not checking them live.
722|CDN kontentni foydalanuvchiga yaqinroq tarmoq nuqtasidan yetkazishi mumkin. Bu kechikishni kamaytiradi, ammo har javob keshlanmasligi kerak: shaxsiy ma’lumotni umumiy keshga qo‘ymang.|A CDN can serve content from network locations nearer users. It may reduce latency, but private responses must not accidentally enter a shared cache.
723|Domain — saytning nomli manzili; hosting — uni ishlatadigan hisoblash va saqlash xizmati. Domenning DNS sozlamasi kerakli xizmatga yo‘naltiradi.|A domain is a named address; hosting supplies the computing and storage running the site. DNS connects the name to the relevant service.
724|DNS domen nomini kerakli yozuvlarga moslaydi. A/AAAA IP manzilga, CNAME boshqa nomga, MX email yo‘nalishiga xizmat qiladi. O‘zgarishlar kesh va TTL sabab darhol hamma joyda ko‘rinmasligi mumkin.|DNS maps domain names to records. A/AAAA indicate IP addresses, CNAME an alias and MX mail routing. Caches and TTL can delay visibility of changes.
725|Environment variable sozlamani koddan ajratadi: masalan, xizmat manzili yoki maxfiy kalit. Har environment variable sir emas, lekin maxfiy qiymatlarni logga yoki brauzer paketiga chiqarmang.|An environment variable separates configuration from code. It may hold a service address or secret. Not every variable is secret, but secret values must stay out of logs and browser bundles.
727|Authentication — kimligingizni tekshirish; authorization — aynan nima qilishga ruxsatingiz borligini tekshirish. Login bo‘lish boshqa foydalanuvchining natijasini ko‘rish vakolati bermaydi.|Authentication verifies identity; authorisation checks what that identity may do. Being logged in does not authorise reading another user’s results.
728|JWT — claimlarni kodlaydigan token formati; imzolangan token yaxlitligini tekshirish mumkin. Oddiy imzolangan JWT payload’i shifrlangan degani emas. Imzo, amal muddati va tegishli issuer/audience tekshirilmasdan role matniga ishonmang.|JWT encodes claims. A signed token can protect integrity, but its payload is not necessarily encrypted. Verify signatures, expiry and applicable issuer/audience before trusting role claims.
729|Cache avval hisoblangan yoki olingan natijani qayta ishlatib xarajat va kechikishni kamaytiradi. Ammo eskirish, invalidation va foydalanuvchi doirasini to‘g‘ri boshqarish kerak.|A cache reuses prior results to reduce cost and latency. Staleness, invalidation and user scope still need explicit handling.
730|Rate limiting ma’lum vaqt ichidagi so‘rovlar soni yoki xarajatini cheklaydi. U yuk va suiiste’molni boshqarishga yordam beradi, lekin autentifikatsiya yoki ruxsatni almashtirmaydi.|Rate limiting bounds requests or cost over time. It helps manage load and abuse but does not replace authentication or authorisation.
731|Python list — elementlari almashtiriladigan ketma-ketlik. Tuple — ketma-ketlik tarkibi o‘zgarmaydigan tur; ichidagi mutable obyekt baribir o‘zgarishi mumkin. Tuple avtomatik chuqur muzlatish emas.|A Python list is mutable; a tuple’s sequence of references is immutable. A mutable object inside a tuple can still change, so a tuple is not deep freezing.
732|Let va const blok doirasiga ega; const o‘zgaruvchini qayta bog‘lashga yo‘l qo‘ymaydi, obyekt ichini avtomatik muzlatmaydi. Var funksiya doirasida ishlaydi va hoisting xulqi farq qiladi.|Let and const are block-scoped. Const prevents rebinding, not mutation of an object’s contents. Var is function-scoped and has different hoisting behaviour.
733|Async/await asinxron ish natijasini kutishni o‘qilishi qulay shaklda yozadi. Kutish CPU hisobini avtomatik parallel qilmaydi. Mustaqil ishlar uchun concurrency va xato/tugash tartibini alohida loyihalang.|Async/await expresses asynchronous waiting clearly. It does not automatically parallelise CPU work. Concurrency and failure/order handling still need deliberate design.
734|Promise — keyinroq muvaffaqiyatli qiymat yoki xato bilan yakunlanadigan asinxron natija ifodasi. Pending, fulfilled yoki rejected holatlari bor. Uni yaratish ishning muvaffaqiyati kafolati emas.|A Promise represents an eventual asynchronous value or failure, with pending, fulfilled and rejected states. Creating one does not guarantee success.
735|Unit test kichik xulqni alohida tekshiradi. Integration test qismlarning birga ishlashini tekshiradi. Haqiqiy brauzer, sessiya va ma’lumot oqimi uchun end-to-end dalil ham kerak bo‘lishi mumkin.|A unit test checks focused behaviour; an integration test checks components working together. Real browser, session and data flows may also need end-to-end evidence.
736|Mock tashqi bog‘liqlik o‘rniga nazorat qilinadigan javob beradi. Xato va chekka holatlarni sinashga qulay, lekin haqiqiy tarmoq yoki database mosligini isbotlamaydi.|A mock replaces a dependency with controlled behaviour, useful for failures and edge cases. It does not prove real network or database compatibility.
737|Container ilova va bog‘liqliklarni izolyatsiyalangan ishlash muhiti sifatida qadoqlaydi. U virtual mashina bilan bir xil emas va xavfsizlikni avtomatik ta’minlamaydi; image, huquqlar va sirlarni boshqarish muhim.|Containers package software and dependencies in isolated execution environments. They are not identical to virtual machines and do not ensure security automatically; images, privileges and secrets matter.
738|Virtual environment Python loyihasining paketlarini boshqa loyihalardan ajratadi. U alohida operatsion tizim yoki xavfsizlik sandboxi emas. Bog‘liqlik versiyalarini ham qayd eting.|A Python virtual environment isolates project packages. It is not a separate operating system or security sandbox. Record dependency versions as well.
739|TypeScript JavaScript’ga statik tip tekshiruvini qo‘shadi. Kattaroq kod bazasida xatoni erta topishga yordam beradi; runtime’dagi begona ma’lumotni baribir tekshirish kerak. Avval JavaScript asoslarini tushunish foydali.|TypeScript adds static type checking to JavaScript. It can catch mistakes earlier, but untrusted runtime data still needs validation. Understanding JavaScript fundamentals remains useful.
740|Machine learning ma’lumotdan qonuniyat o‘rganadigan usullar oilasi. Deep learning — ko‘p qatlamli neyron tarmoqlarga tayangan qismi. Har ML masalasi katta neyron model talab qilmaydi.|Machine learning covers methods that learn patterns from data. Deep learning is a subset based on multilayer neural networks. Not every problem needs a large neural model.
741|LLM — katta hajmdagi til ma’lumotlari bilan o‘qitilgan til modeli. U ketma-ketlik asosida matn hosil qiladi; bilim yoki to‘g‘rilikni kafolatlamaydi. RIWI’ning hozirgi qoidaviy mexanizmi LLM o‘qitildi degani emas.|An LLM is a language model trained on large amounts of text. It generates sequences without guaranteeing correctness. RIWI’s current rule-based mechanism is not an LLM trained by uploading these questions.
742|RAG javobdan oldin tegishli ma’lumotni qidirib, unga tayangan holda javob tayyorlash usulidir. Topilgan matn noto‘g‘ri yoki ruxsatsiz bo‘lsa, natija ham muammoli bo‘ladi; retrievalning o‘zi haqiqat kafolati emas.|RAG retrieves relevant material before producing an answer. Incorrect or unauthorised retrieved material can still lead to problems; retrieval alone does not establish truth.
743|Chatbot asosan suhbatga javob beradi. Agent maqsad yo‘lida vosita yoki bir necha qadamni boshqarishi mumkin; atamalar doim bir xil ishlatilmaydi. Vosita borligi xavfsiz mustaqil ishlash vakolati bor degani emas.|A chatbot mainly responds conversationally; an agent may coordinate tools or steps towards a goal. Terminology varies. Tool access does not itself grant unrestricted authority.
744|Yaxshi topshiriqda maqsad, kirish ma’lumoti, cheklov va kutilgan chiqish aniq yoziladi. Natijani bir xil sinov misollarida tekshirib, dalilsiz ishonchni emas, to‘g‘rilikni baholang.|A useful prompt states the goal, input, constraints and expected output. Evaluate results on consistent examples rather than mistaking confident language for correctness.
745|Hallucination — modelning ishonchli ohangda noto‘g‘ri yoki o‘ylab topilgan ma’lumot berishi. Sana, hisob, havola va muhim da’volarni mustaqil tekshiring. Chiroyli yozilgan javob dalil emas.|A hallucination is a plausible-looking but false or invented output. Independently check dates, calculations, links and consequential claims. Fluent wording is not evidence.
746|AI javobini vazifa bo‘yicha tekshiring: fakt to‘g‘rimi, savolga mosmi, ruxsat saqlanganmi, yetishmagan ma’lumot tan olinganmi? Oddiy, noaniq, xatoli yozuvli va xavfsizlik misollarini alohida sinang.|Evaluate factual accuracy, relevance, permissions and handling of missing information. Include normal, ambiguous, misspelled and adversarial cases rather than only easy examples.
749|Kichik xatoni tanlang, loyiha yo‘riqnomasini o‘qing, mavjud testni ishga tushiring va minimal o‘zgarish taklif qiling. PR’da muammo, natijadagi xulq va test dalilini yozing. Hali yubormagan ishni yuborildi deb aytmang.|Choose a small issue, read the project guidance, run relevant tests and propose a minimal change. Explain the problem, resulting behaviour and validation in the PR. Do not claim an unsubmitted change was sent.
750|Uch oylik namunaviy yo‘l: birinchi oy — til asoslari, Git va kichik CLI; ikkinchi oy — HTTP, API, database va ruxsatlar; uchinchi oy — test, log, deploy va bitta yakuniy loyiha. Haftalik vaqtni aytsangiz hajmni moslash mumkin. Bu ishga kirish kafolati emas.|An illustrative three-month path: month one language fundamentals, Git and a small CLI; month two HTTP, APIs, databases and permissions; month three tests, logs, deployment and one complete project. Adjust to available weekly time; this is not an employment guarantee.'''
for line in TECH.splitlines():
    number,uz,en=line.split('|');add('tech-'+number,'base:'+number,uz,en)

add('career-start','base:751,752,753,754,757,758,759,761,762,780,798',
 'Kasb tanlashda qiziqish, mavjud ko‘nikma, haqiqiy vakansiya talabi va o‘rganish imkonini solishtiring; kelajak daromadini kafolatlab bo‘lmaydi. Portfolio’da 1–2 tugallangan loyiha, siz bajargan qism, qarorlar va natijani ko‘rsating. Intervyuda bilmasangiz, taxminni belgilang va qanday tekshirishingizni ayting. Ish qidirishda rasmiy e’lon va ish beruvchi shaxsini tekshiring; ish olish uchun shubhali oldindan to‘lovga rozi bo‘lmang.',
 'Compare interests, existing skills, real job requirements and learning capacity; no future income is guaranteed. A portfolio should show one or two completed projects, your contribution, decisions and evidence. In interviews, distinguish what you know from a hypothesis and explain how you would verify it. Check employers and be cautious about paying to obtain a job.')
add('cv-cover','base:755,756',
 'Resume odatda ma’lum ishga mos qisqa tajriba va natijalar bayoni. CV atamasi mamlakat va sohaga qarab batafsil akademik hujjat yoki resume ma’nosida ishlatiladi. Cover letter’da qaysi rol, nega mosligingiz va bitta aniq dalilni yozing: «I am applying for the junior developer role. In my recent project, I built…» Tajriba va natijani uydirmang.',
 'A resume is usually a concise, role-focused account of experience and results. CV usage varies by country and field, from an academic record to a synonym for resume. A cover letter names the role, your fit and specific evidence: I am applying for the junior developer role. In my recent project, I built… Never invent achievements.')
add('business-validation','base:765,766,767,768,770,785,786,787,793,797',
 'Avval kimning qaysi muammosini yechayotganingizni aniqlang. Taxminni kichik sinovga aylantiring: suhbat, oddiy prototip yoki bitta cheklangan xizmat. MVP — asosiy taxminni tekshirishga yetadigan eng kichik ishlaydigan yechim; sifatsiz hamma funksiya emas. Mijoz qaytishi, foyda va xizmat xarajatini o‘lchang; faqat maqtov yoki ro‘yxatdan o‘tish yetmaydi.',
 'Identify the customer and problem, then test one assumption through interviews, a prototype or a small service. An MVP is the smallest usable approach that tests the key assumption, not every feature done poorly. Measure repeat use, value and delivery cost rather than treating compliments or sign-ups as proof of fit.')
add('pricing','base:760,769,782',
 'Narxni kelishishda ish hajmi, topshiriladigan natija, muddat, tuzatishlar soni va to‘lov shartini yozma aniqlang. Xarajat va yetkazish vaqtini hisoblamasdan faqat raqobatchi narxini ko‘chirmang. Oldindan to‘lov riskni kamaytirishi mumkin, lekin ikki tomon uchun qaytarish va bekor qilish sharti aniq bo‘lsin. Bu shartnoma yoki huquqiy xulosa o‘rnini bosmaydi.',
 'Define scope, deliverables, deadline, revision limits and payment terms in writing. Estimate delivery time and cost rather than copying a competitor’s price. A deposit can reduce risk, but cancellation and refund terms need clarity for both sides. This is general education, not a contract or legal determination.')
add('revenue-profit','base:771,772',
 'Daromad — sotuvdan tushgan summa; foyda — tegishli xarajatlar ayirilgandan qolgan natija. Pul oqimi esa pulning amalda kirishi va chiqishi. Masalan, 1 mln so‘mlik sotuv va 700 ming xarajat — 300 ming foyda; mijoz hali to‘lamagan bo‘lsa, kassada bu pul bo‘lmasligi mumkin.',
 'Revenue is sales income; profit subtracts the relevant costs. Cash flow tracks actual cash receipts and payments. Sales of 1,000 with costs of 700 yield profit of 300, but if the customer has not paid, the cash may not yet be available.')
add('break-even','base:773',
 'Oddiy modelda zararsizlik hajmi = doimiy xarajat ÷ (birlik narxi − birlik o‘zgaruvchan xarajati). Masalan, 1 000 000 ÷ (50 000 − 30 000) = 50 birlik. Bu faqat narx va xarajat o‘zgarmas, barcha birlik sotiladi degan farazdagi hisob; haqiqiy biznesda soliq, qaytarish va quvvat cheklovi ham bor.',
 'In a simple model, break-even units equal fixed costs divided by price minus variable cost per unit. For example, 1,000,000 / (50,000 − 30,000) = 50 units. This assumes constant costs/prices and saleable output; real taxes, returns and capacity can alter the result.')
add('budget','base:774,775,776,779',
 'Budjetda tasdiqlangan tushum, zarur xarajatlar, o‘zgaruvchan xarajat va kutilmagan holat uchun zaxirani ajrating. Qarzda faqat oylik to‘lov emas, jami qaytarish, komissiya, muddat va daromad kamayishi xavfini ham solishtiring. Hammaga mos qat’iy foiz yoki qarz olish tavsiyasi yo‘q; shaxsiy qaror uchun to‘liq shartlar va malakali maslahat kerak.',
 'Separate verified income, essential costs, variable spending and a contingency reserve. For borrowing, compare total repayment, fees, term and income-loss risk, not just the monthly instalment. There is no universal allocation or borrowing recommendation; personal decisions require the full terms and appropriate qualified advice.')
add('inflation','base:777',
 'Inflyatsiya narxlarning umumiy darajasi oshishini anglatadi; shu pulga olinadigan mahsulot kamayishi mumkin. Nominal o‘sish bilan xarid qobiliyati bir xil emas. Masalan, pul 5% ko‘payib, narxlar 10% oshsa, real xarid qobiliyati taxminan 1.05/1.10−1 ≈ −4.5% bo‘ladi. Bu misol, joriy inflyatsiya prognozi emas.',
 'Inflation is an increase in the general price level, which can reduce purchasing power. Nominal growth differs from real growth: a 5% balance increase with 10% inflation gives about 1.05/1.10 − 1 = −4.5% real change. This is an illustration, not a current forecast.')
add('compound','base:778',
 'Murakkab foizda keyingi davr foizi oldingi foiz qo‘shilgan summaga hisoblanadi. Oddiy formulada A=P(1+r)^n. Masalan, 1 000 birlik, yillik 10%, ikki yil: 1 000×1.1²=1 210. Bu o‘zgarmas stavka, komissiyasiz va soliqsiz misol; haqiqiy mahsulot daromadi kafolati emas.',
 'Compound interest applies interest to a balance that includes earlier interest. In a simple model A=P(1+r)^n: 1,000 at 10% annually for two years becomes 1,210. This assumes a fixed rate with no fees or taxes and is not a product-return guarantee.')
add('transparency','base:781,791,794,796',
 'Kim nima uchun javobgar, qanday xarajat va natija kutiladi, qaror qanday o‘lchanadi — shularni oldindan yozing. Sheriklikda ulush, vazifa, pul yechish, kelishmovchilik va chiqish tartibini muhokama qiling. Xodim olishda takroriy ish hajmi va uni moliyalashtirish imkonini tekshiring. Umumiy tavsiya shaxsiy huquqiy yoki moliyaviy ekspertiza o‘rnini bosmaydi.',
 'Record responsibilities, costs, expected outcomes and decision measures. Partners should discuss ownership, duties, withdrawals, disputes and exits. Before hiring, verify recurring workload and funding capacity. General guidance does not replace individual legal or financial review.')
add('marketing','base:783,784,795',
 'Marketing ehtiyoj va auditoriyani tushunib, taklifga qiziqish uyg‘otadi; sotuv esa muayyan kelishuvga olib boradi. Kontent marketing foydali material orqali tegishli auditoriyani jalb qiladi. Kichik sinovda kanal xarajati, sifatli murojaat va haqiqiy sotuvni birga o‘lchang; ko‘rishlar sonining o‘zi foyda emas.',
 'Marketing understands needs and attracts the relevant audience; sales turns an opportunity into an agreement. Content marketing uses useful material to reach that audience. Measure channel cost, qualified enquiries and actual sales together; views alone are not profit.')
add('swot-kpi','base:788,789,790',
 'SWOT ichki kuchli/zaif tomonlar va tashqi imkoniyat/xavflarni ajratadi. KPI — kuzatiladigan natija ko‘rsatkichi; OKR — maqsad va uni ko‘rsatuvchi asosiy natijalar. Masalan, «xatolarni kamaytirish» maqsadi uchun takroriy xato ulushini haftalik o‘lchash mumkin. Raqamni o‘zi uchun oshirish emas, maqsadga xizmat qilishini tekshiring.',
 'SWOT separates internal strengths/weaknesses from external opportunities/threats. A KPI measures performance; an OKR links an objective to measurable key results. For reducing repeat errors, track their weekly rate. Check whether a metric serves the objective rather than optimising the number alone.')

MATH='''801|Foiz «yuzdan ulush» degani. A ning p foizi = A×p/100. Masalan, 80 ning 25 foizi: 80×25/100=20.|Percent means per hundred. p percent of A is A×p/100; for example, 25% of 80 is 20.
802|200 ning 15 foizi 30: 200×15/100=30. Tekshirish: 10 foizi 20, 5 foizi 10; jami 30.|15% of 200 is 30: 200×15/100. Check: 10% is 20 and 5% is 10, totalling 30.
803|Kasrlarni qo‘shishda maxrajni tenglashtiring. 1/2+1/3 = 3/6+2/6 = 5/6. Surat va maxrajni alohida qo‘shish xato.|Use a common denominator: 1/2+1/3=3/6+2/6=5/6. Do not add denominators directly.
804|Kasrni o‘nli ko‘rinishga aylantirish uchun suratni maxrajga bo‘ling: 3/4=0.75. Ayrim kasrlar davriy: 1/3=0.333… . Maxraj nol bo‘la olmaydi.|Divide numerator by denominator: 3/4=0.75; some decimals repeat, such as 1/3=0.333… . The denominator cannot be zero.
805|Proporsiya ikki nisbat tengligi: a/b=c/d. Nol bo‘lmagan maxrajlarda ad=bc. Masalan, 2/3=4/6.|A proportion equates two ratios: a/b=c/d. With nonzero denominators, ad=bc; for example, 2/3=4/6.
806|3:5 ikki qism nisbatidir: birinchi qism 3 ulush, ikkinchisi 5 ulush. Jami 8 ulush; jami 40 bo‘lsa qismlar 15 va 25.|3:5 compares two parts, three shares to five. The total is eight shares; a total of 40 splits into 15 and 25.
807|Tenglamada ikki tomonga bir xil ruxsatli amalni bajaring. 2x+3=11 → 2x=8 → x=4. Tekshirish: 2×4+3=11.|Apply the same valid operation to both sides: 2x+3=11 gives 2x=8, then x=4. Substitute back to check.
808|ax²+bx+c=0 da a≠0 va D=b²−4ac. D>0 — ikkita turli real ildiz; D=0 — bitta takroriy real ildiz; D<0 — real ildiz yo‘q. Kompleks sonlarda yechim bo‘lishi mumkin.|For ax²+bx+c=0 with a≠0, D=b²−4ac. Positive D gives two distinct real roots, zero a repeated real root, and negative D no real roots, though complex roots exist.
809|Funksiya har bir ruxsatli kirish qiymatiga aynan bitta chiqish qiymatini moslaydi. Grafik (x,f(x)) nuqtalarini ko‘rsatadi. Masalan, f(x)=2x bo‘lsa x=3 uchun f(3)=6.|A function assigns exactly one output to each allowed input. Its graph shows points (x,f(x)); for f(x)=2x, f(3)=6.
810|y=mx+b da m — qiyalik: x bir birlik oshganda y qancha o‘zgaradi. Masalan, y=3x+2 da x 1 ga oshsa y 3 ga oshadi.|In y=mx+b, m is the slope: the change in y per unit change in x. For y=3x+2, y increases by 3 when x increases by 1.
811|To‘g‘ri burchakli uchburchakda a²+b²=c²; c — gipotenuza. Katetlar 3 va 4 bo‘lsa c=√(9+16)=5. Bu qoida har qanday uchburchakka shu shaklda tatbiq qilinmaydi.|For a right triangle, a²+b²=c², with c the hypotenuse. Legs 3 and 4 give c=5. This form requires a right angle.
812|Uchburchak yuzi asos×shu asosga perpendikulyar balandlik÷2. Asos 8 sm, balandlik 5 sm bo‘lsa yuzi 20 sm².|Triangle area is base times perpendicular height divided by two. A base of 8 cm and height of 5 cm give 20 cm².
813|Aylana uzunligi C=2πr=πd. Radius 3 sm bo‘lsa C=6π sm, taxminan 18.85 sm.|Circumference is C=2πr=πd. Radius 3 cm gives 6π cm, about 18.85 cm.
814|Radius markazdan aylanagacha masofa; diametr markazdan o‘tib ikki chetni birlashtiradi. Diametr radiusning ikki baravari: d=2r.|A radius runs from centre to circle; a diameter passes through the centre between opposite points. d=2r.
815|Kub hajmi V=a³. Qirra 4 sm bo‘lsa V=64 sm³. Hajm birliklari kub birliklarda yoziladi.|Cube volume is V=a³. A 4 cm edge gives 64 cm³; volume uses cubic units.
816|O‘rtacha — yig‘indi sonlar soniga bo‘linadi. Mediana — tartiblangan ro‘yxatning o‘rtasi. 1,2,9 da o‘rtacha 4, mediana 2; katta chekka qiymat o‘rtachaga kuchliroq ta’sir qiladi.|The mean is sum divided by count; the median is the middle of ordered values. For 1,2,9, the mean is 4 and median 2. An extreme value affects the mean more strongly.
817|Moda — eng ko‘p takrorlangan qiymat. 2,2,3,4 da moda 2. Bir nechta moda yoki barcha qiymat bir xil chastotada bo‘lsa yagona moda bo‘lmasligi mumkin.|The mode is the most frequent value: 2 in 2,2,3,4. Data may have multiple modes or no unique mode.
818|Teng ehtimolli natijalarda ehtimollik = qulay natijalar soni ÷ jami natijalar soni. Adolatli kubikda 6 tushish ehtimoli 1/6. Teng ehtimollilik farazini tekshirish kerak.|For equally likely outcomes, probability is favourable outcomes divided by total outcomes. A fair die gives probability 1/6 of rolling a six. The equal-likelihood assumption matters.
819|Ikki mustaqil adolatli tangada ikkisi ham gerb: 1/2×1/2=1/4, ya’ni 25%. Natijalar GG, GR, RG, RR; ulardan bittasi GG.|For two independent fair coins, both heads has probability 1/2×1/2=1/4=25%. Of HH, HT, TH, TT, only HH qualifies.
820|Permutatsiyada tartib muhim; kombinatsiyada tanlangan guruh muhim, tartib emas. A,B dan AB va BA ikki tartib, lekin bitta ikki kishilik guruh.|Permutations distinguish order; combinations do not. AB and BA are two arrangements but the same two-member group.
821|logₐ(b)=c degani aᶜ=b. Masalan, log₂(8)=3, chunki 2³=8. Real logarifm uchun asos a>0, a≠1 va b>0.|logₐ(b)=c means aᶜ=b. For example, log₂8=3 because 2³=8. For real logs, a>0, a≠1 and b>0.
822|Hosila funksiyaning nuqtadagi o‘zgarish tezligini, grafikda urinma qiyaligini bildiradi. f(x)=x² uchun f′(x)=2x; x=3 da qiyalik 6.|A derivative measures local rate of change or tangent slope. For f(x)=x², f′(x)=2x, so the slope at x=3 is 6.
823|Integral uzluksiz miqdorlarni yig‘ish g‘oyasidir. Aniq integral ishorali maydon yoki o‘zgarishdan jami miqdorni topishi mumkin. Masalan, doimiy tezlikni vaqt bo‘yicha integrallash masofani beradi.|Integration accumulates continuous quantities. A definite integral can give signed area or total change; integrating constant speed over time gives distance.
824|Vaqt murakkabligi kirish hajmi oshganda amallar soni qanday o‘sishini tasvirlaydi. Ro‘yxatni bir marta ko‘rish odatda O(n); har bir elementni har biri bilan solishtirish O(n²) bo‘lishi mumkin. Bu aniq millisekund emas.|Time complexity describes growth in operations with input size. One traversal is typically O(n); comparing every pair may be O(n²). It is not an exact millisecond prediction.
825|Premissa — xulosa chiqarishda asos sifatida olingan gap. Mantiqan to‘g‘ri shaklning o‘zi premissalar fakt sifatida to‘g‘riligini isbotlamaydi.|A premise is a statement used to support a conclusion. A valid inference form does not itself prove its premises are factually true.
826|Yo‘q. Barcha A lar B bo‘lishi barcha B lar A degani emas. Masalan, barcha mushuklar hayvon, ammo barcha hayvonlar mushuk emas.|No. All A being B does not imply all B are A. All cats are animals, but not all animals are cats.
827|Paradoks — bir qarashda asosli fikrlardan qarama-qarshi yoki kutilmagan natija chiqishi. Bu ta’rif, faraz yoki mantiqdagi yashirin muammoni tekshirishga undaydi.|A paradox is an apparently contradictory or surprising result from seemingly reasonable reasoning. It invites examination of assumptions, definitions or logic.
828|Korrelyatsiya ikki miqdorning birga o‘zgarishi; sababiyat biri ikkinchisiga ta’sir qilishidir. Muzqaymoq va cho‘milish ko‘payishi issiq ob-havo bilan bog‘liq bo‘lishi mumkin; biri boshqasini keltirib chiqardi degani emas.|Correlation is co-variation; causation means one factor influences another. Ice-cream sales and swimming may both rise in hot weather without one causing the other.
829|Inersial sanoq sistemasida natijaviy kuch nol bo‘lsa, jism tinch yoki o‘zgarmas tezlik bilan to‘g‘ri chiziqli harakatda qoladi. Kuch yo‘qligi harakat ham yo‘q degani emas.|In an inertial frame, zero net force means rest or uniform straight-line motion. No net force does not imply no motion.
830|O‘zgarmas massa uchun Nyutonning ikkinchi qonuni F=ma: natijaviy kuch massa va tezlanish ko‘paytmasi. 2 kg jismga 6 N net kuch ta’sir etsa, a=3 m/s².|For constant mass, Newton’s second law is F=ma. A net force of 6 N on 2 kg gives acceleration 3 m/s².
831|Yopiq tizimda jami energiya saqlanadi, ammo shakli o‘zgaradi. Masalan, tushayotgan jismning potensial energiyasi kinetik energiyaga, ishqalanishda esa issiqlikka aylanadi.|Total energy in a closed system is conserved while changing form. Falling converts potential to kinetic energy; friction transfers energy into thermal forms.
832|Quyosh nuri atmosferada sochiladi. Qisqaroq ko‘k to‘lqinlar uzunroq qizil to‘lqinlarga qaraganda kuchliroq sochilgani uchun osmon ko‘pincha ko‘k ko‘rinadi. Bu dengiz rangining oddiy aksi emas.|Sunlight scatters in the atmosphere. Shorter blue wavelengths scatter more strongly than longer red wavelengths, making much of the daytime sky appear blue. It is not simply an ocean reflection.
833|Tezlik masofa/vaqt bilan o‘lchanadi: SI birligi m/s. Vakuumdagi yorug‘lik tezligi aniq 299 792 458 m/s. Moddadagi tarqalish tezligi bundan boshqacha bo‘lishi mumkin.|Speed is distance per time, measured in m/s in SI. Light in vacuum travels at exactly 299,792,458 m/s; propagation in a material can differ.
834|Oddiy tovush mexanik tebranish bo‘lib, tarqalishi uchun muhit kerak. Ideal vakuumda u tarqalmaydi. Elektromagnit to‘lqinlar esa vakuumda tarqala oladi.|Ordinary sound is a mechanical disturbance requiring a medium and does not propagate through an ideal vacuum. Electromagnetic waves can travel through vacuum.
835|Atom kimyoviy elementning xususiyatini saqlovchi birlik. Molekula bog‘langan atomlardan tuzilgan birlik. Masalan, suv molekulasi ikki vodorod va bitta kislorod atomidan iborat.|An atom is a unit of a chemical element; a molecule consists of bonded atoms. A water molecule contains two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom.
836|Elektr toki — zaryad oqimi, amperda o‘lchanadi. Kuchlanish — birlik zaryadga to‘g‘ri keladigan potensial energiya farqi, voltda. Ularni bir xil kattalik deb qabul qilmang.|Current is the rate of charge flow, measured in amperes. Voltage is electric potential difference, measured in volts. They are different quantities.
837|Kislota va asos xossalari indikator yoki mos o‘lchov bilan tekshiriladi. Noma’lum moddani tatib ko‘rish yoki uyda aralashtirib sinash xavfli. Tajriba faqat xavfsiz laboratoriya tartibida bajariladi.|Acid/base properties can be checked with suitable indicators or measurement. Never taste or casually mix unknown chemicals. Experiments require an appropriate safety procedure.
838|pH eritmaning kislotaliligini ifodalaydi; vodorod ionlari faolligi bilan logarifmik bog‘liq. Suyultirilgan suvli eritmada 25°C atrofida pH 7 neytral, pastrog‘i kislotali, yuqorirog‘i asosli. Sharoit muhim.|pH is a logarithmic measure related to hydrogen-ion activity. For dilute aqueous solutions around 25°C, pH 7 is neutral, lower values acidic and higher values basic. Conditions matter.
839|Fotosintezda o‘simlik, suvo‘t va ayrim bakteriyalar yorug‘lik energiyasini kimyoviy energiyaga aylantiradi. O‘simliklarda karbonat angidrid va suvdan organik modda hosil bo‘lib, kislorod ajraladi.|Photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy. In plants, carbon dioxide and water contribute to organic compounds while oxygen is released.
840|Yadro eukariot hujayrada DNKning katta qismini saqlaydi va gen ifodasi orqali faoliyatni boshqarishda qatnashadi. Barcha hujayralarda yadro bor emas; bakteriyalarda membranali yadro yo‘q.|The nucleus stores most DNA in eukaryotic cells and participates in regulating activity through gene expression. Not all cells have one; bacteria lack a membrane-bound nucleus.
841|DNK odatda irsiy ma’lumotni uzoqroq saqlaydi; RNK uning ifodalanishi va oqsil sintezi kabi ishlarda qatnashadi. DNKda dezoksiriboza va timin, RNKda riboza va uratsil bo‘ladi; shaklida istisnolar bor.|DNA usually stores hereditary information; RNA participates in expression and protein synthesis among other roles. DNA contains deoxyribose and thymine; RNA ribose and uracil. Structural exceptions exist.
842|Evolyutsiya — populyatsiyalardagi irsiy xususiyatlar avlodlar davomida o‘zgarishi. Tabiiy tanlanish, mutatsiya, gen oqimi va genetik drift kabi jarayonlar qatnashadi; alohida odamning umr davomida mashq bilan o‘zgarishi bilan bir xil emas.|Evolution is change in inherited characteristics of populations over generations through processes including selection, mutation, gene flow and drift. It is not the same as an individual improving through practice.
843|Immun tizimi begona omillarni tanish va ularga javob berishda qatnashuvchi hujayra hamda molekulalar tizimidir. Tug‘ma va orttirilgan javoblar hamkorlik qiladi. Bu umumiy ta’rif, shaxsiy kasallik yoki davolash bo‘yicha tashxis emas.|The immune system uses cells and molecules to recognise and respond to threats. Innate and adaptive responses work together. This is a general definition, not individual diagnosis or treatment advice.
844|Quyosh tortishishi sayyora harakati yo‘nalishini egadi, uning harakati esa orbitada davom etadi. Orbitani «tortishish yo‘q» deb tushunish xato; u erkin tushishning bir shakli.|Solar gravity continuously curves planetary motion into an orbit. Orbiting does not mean gravity is absent; it is a form of free fall.
845|Oy doim taxminan yarim yoritilgan, ammo Yerga ko‘rinadigan yoritilgan qism uning orbitadagi holati bilan o‘zgaradi. Odatdagi fazalar Yer soyasi sababli emas; Yer soyasi Oy tutilishida qatnashadi.|About half the Moon is illuminated; the fraction of that lit half visible from Earth changes with orbital position. Ordinary phases are not caused by Earth’s shadow, which matters during a lunar eclipse.
846|Qora tuynuk — fazo-vaqtning voqea gorizonti ichidan yorug‘lik ham tashqariga chiqa olmaydigan sohasi. Uni hamma narsani har qanday masofadan so‘rib oladigan oddiy changyutgich deb tasvirlash to‘g‘ri emas.|A black hole is a region whose event horizon prevents even light from escaping outward. It is not a vacuum cleaner that pulls in everything at any distance.
847|Ob-havo — qisqa muddatdagi atmosfera holati. Iqlim — uzoq davrdagi statistik xususiyatlar va o‘zgaruvchanlik. Bir kunning sovuqligi uzoq muddatli global yo‘nalishni inkor qilmaydi.|Weather is the short-term atmospheric state; climate concerns long-term statistics and variability. One cold day does not disprove a long-term global trend.
848|Hozirgi global isishning asosiy omili inson faoliyati, ayniqsa qazilma yoqilg‘i va yer foydalanishi bilan bog‘liq issiqxona gazlaridir. Gazlar Yerning chiqayotgan issiqligini ushlab qolish jarayoniga ta’sir qiladi.|The main driver of current global warming is human activity, especially greenhouse-gas emissions linked to fossil fuels and land use. These gases affect the escape of outgoing heat.
849|Ilmiy nazariya ko‘p dalil bilan asoslangan tushuntirish tizimi; «shunchaki taxmin» emas. Gipoteza — tekshirish mumkin bo‘lgan taklif. Ikkalasi ham yangi dalilga qarab qayta baholanadi.|A scientific theory is a well-supported explanatory framework, not merely a guess. A hypothesis is a testable proposal. Both are assessed against evidence.
850|Da’voni o‘lchanadigan taxminga aylantiring, nazorat va taqqoslash shartini belgilang, oldindan natija mezonini yozing va tajribani takrorlang. Bitta tasodifiy natija umumiy sababni isbotlamaydi.|Turn a claim into a measurable prediction, define controls and comparison, state outcome criteria in advance and repeat the test. A single chance result does not establish a general cause.'''
for line in MATH.splitlines():
    number,uz,en=line.split('|');add('science-'+number,'base:'+number,uz,en)

HISTORY='''901|O‘zbekiston poytaxti — Toshkent. U Toshkent viloyatidan alohida ma’muriy birlik bo‘lgan shahardir.|Uzbekistan’s capital is Tashkent, a city administratively separate from Tashkent Region.
902|O‘zbekistonda 12 viloyat bor. Qoraqalpog‘iston Respublikasi va Toshkent shahri alohida birliklar; ularni «yana ikki viloyat» deb qo‘shish noto‘g‘ri.|Uzbekistan has 12 regions. The Republic of Karakalpakstan and Tashkent City are separate units, not two additional regions.
903|Namangan Farg‘ona vodiysidagi hunarmandchilik, bog‘dorchilik va gulchilik an’analari bilan tanilgan. Aniq sayr joyi, ish vaqti yoki yo‘l holatini jonli tekshirish kerak; men hozir buni tekshirmayapman.|Namangan, in the Fergana Valley, is associated with crafts, horticulture and flower-growing traditions. Specific venues, hours and travel conditions require current verification.
904|Registon Samarqanddagi tarixiy maydon bo‘lib, Ulug‘bek, Sherdor va Tillakori madrasalari majmuasi bilan tanilgan. Ular turli davrlarda qurilgan; butun majmuani bir hukmdor bir vaqtda qurgan deb aytish xato.|Registan is Samarkand’s historic square, known for the Ulugh Beg, Sher-Dor and Tilla-Kari madrasahs, built in different periods rather than all at once by one ruler.
905|Buxorodagi mashhur obidalarga Somoniylar maqbarasi, Kalon minorasi va masjidi, Mir Arab madrasasi hamda Ark kiradi. Bu namunaviy ro‘yxat; tashrif vaqti va chipta shartlari alohida tekshiriladi.|Examples of Bukhara landmarks include the Samanid Mausoleum, Kalyan Minaret and Mosque, Mir-i Arab Madrasah and the Ark. Visiting hours and ticket terms require separate checks.
906|Ichan-qal’a — Xivaning devor bilan o‘ralgan ichki shahri. Masjid, madrasa, saroy va turar joylar tarixiy shahar muhitini tashkil qiladi. U 1990-yilda Jahon merosi ro‘yxatiga kiritilgan.|Itchan Kala is Khiva’s walled inner town, combining mosques, madrasahs, palaces and homes. It entered the World Heritage List in 1990.
907|Buyuk Ipak yo‘li bitta yo‘l emas, savdo va aloqa tarmoqlari edi. Tovarlar bilan birga bilim, din, texnologiya va san’at g‘oyalari ham hududlar o‘rtasida tarqalgan.|The Silk Roads were networks of trade and communication rather than a single road. Goods travelled alongside knowledge, religions, technologies and artistic ideas.
908|Amir Temur 1336–1405-yillarda yashagan. U XIV asr oxiri va XV asr boshida katta davlat tuzgan; tarixiy faoliyatini o‘sha davr siyosiy va harbiy sharoitida ko‘rish kerak.|Amir Timur lived from 1336 to 1405 and built a large state in the late fourteenth and early fifteenth centuries. His actions need their historical political and military context.
909|Mirzo Ulug‘bek astronomiya va matematikaga, ayniqsa Samarqand rasadxonasi hamda yulduzlar katalogi bilan bog‘liq kuzatuvlarga hissa qo‘shgan. Bu ishlar jamoaviy ilmiy muhitda amalga oshirilgan.|Ulugh Beg contributed to astronomy and mathematics through the Samarkand observatory and associated stellar observations and catalogue, within a collaborative scholarly community.
910|Al-Xorazmiy algebra va hisob usullarining rivojlanishidagi asarlari bilan tanilgan. «Algoritm» atamasi uning ismining lotinlashtirilgan shakli bilan bog‘liq. Uni barcha matematikaning yagona yaratuvchisi deb aytish to‘g‘ri emas.|Al-Khwarizmi is known for influential work on algebra and calculation. Algorithm derives from a Latinised form of his name. He was not the sole inventor of all mathematics.
911|Ibn Sinoning mashhur asarlaridan «Tib qonunlari» va «Kitob ash-Shifo» bor. Ikkinchisi faqat davolash qo‘llanmasi emas, keng falsafiy-ilmiy asardir. Tarixiy tibbiy matn zamonaviy davolash tavsiyasi o‘rnini bosmaydi.|Ibn Sina’s works include The Canon of Medicine and The Book of Healing, the latter a broad philosophical/scientific work rather than merely a treatment manual. Historical medicine is not current clinical advice.
912|Alisher Navoiy chig‘atoy turkiysidagi adabiyotni yuksaltirgan, g‘azal va dostonlarda axloq, muhabbat va insoniy kamolot mavzularini yoritgan. «Xamsa» uning muhim asarlar turkumidir.|Alisher Navoi developed Chagatai Turkic literature through poetry and narrative works on love, ethics and human development. His Khamsa is a major cycle of works.
913|O‘zbek tili turkiy tillar oilasining qarluq guruhiga mansub. Boshqa turkiy tillar bilan o‘xshashlik bo‘lsa ham, ularning barchasi bir xil yoki to‘liq o‘zaro tushunarli emas.|Uzbek belongs to the Karluk branch of Turkic languages. Related languages share features but are not identical or necessarily fully mutually intelligible.
914|Lotin va kirill — yozuv tizimlari; o‘zbek tili ikkalasida ham yoziladi. Harflarni ko‘chirish har doim oddiy birga-bir almashtirish emas: ё/ю/я, tutuq va o‘/g‘ kabi holatlar kontekst talab qilishi mumkin.|Latin and Cyrillic are writing systems used for Uzbek. Transliteration is not always a simple one-to-one substitution; combinations and apostrophe-related letters can require context.
915|O‘zbekiston mustaqilligi 1991-yil 31-avgustda e’lon qilingan. 1-sentabr Mustaqillik kuni sifatida nishonlanadi. E’lon qilingan sana va bayram sanasini ajrating.|Uzbekistan’s independence was proclaimed on 31 August 1991; Independence Day is celebrated on 1 September. Distinguish the proclamation date from the holiday.
916|Navro‘z, Mustaqillik kuni va Konstitutsiya kuni davlat bayramlari misollaridir. Ko‘chirilgan dam olish kunlari va diniy bayramning aynan qaysi sanaga to‘g‘ri kelishi yilga qarab rasmiy taqvimdan tekshiriladi; men joriy ish taqvimini jonli tekshirmayapman.|Examples include Navruz, Independence Day and Constitution Day. Transferred days off and specific religious-holiday dates need that year’s official calendar; I am not checking a live work calendar.
917|Navro‘z bahor va yangilanish bilan bog‘liq qadimiy bayramdir. U turli mamlakat va jamoalarda o‘ziga xos urf-odatlar bilan nishonlanadi; faqat bir xalq yoki bitta taom bilan cheklanmaydi.|Navruz is an ancient celebration associated with spring and renewal, observed with varied customs across countries and communities rather than belonging to only one people or dish.
918|O‘zbek taomlariga osh, manti, somsa, sho‘rva va norin misol bo‘ladi. Tayyorlash usullari hudud va oilaga qarab farqlanadi; bitta retseptni yagona to‘g‘ri shakl deb ko‘rsatish shart emas.|Examples include plov, manti, samsa, shurpa and norin. Recipes vary by region and family; there need not be one uniquely correct version.
919|Atlas odatda ipakli, silliq yaltiroq to‘qilish bilan; adras esa an’anaviy holda ipak va paxta aralashmasi bilan tanilgan. Mahsulot tarkibi zamonaviy ishlab chiqarishda farq qilishi mumkin, shuning uchun yorliqni tekshiring.|Atlas is associated with smooth, lustrous silk weaving; adras traditionally combines silk and cotton. Modern products can differ, so check the actual fabric label.
920|Yirik daryo tizimlariga Amudaryo va Sirdaryo kiradi. Ular chegaralar bo‘ylab va bir necha davlat hududida oqadi; suv masalasi faqat bitta viloyat doirasiga tegishli emas.|Major river systems include the Amu Darya and Syr Darya, which cross or follow borders among several countries. Their water systems extend beyond one region.
921|Orol dengizining keskin qisqarishida uni to‘ldiruvchi daryolar suvining sug‘orishga katta hajmda burilishi asosiy rol o‘ynagan. Bug‘lanish va mintaqaviy sharoit ham suv balansiga ta’sir qiladi. Bu oddiy «tabiiy ravishda yo‘qolgan» hodisa emas.|Large-scale diversion of feeder-river water for irrigation was central to the Aral Sea’s shrinkage. Evaporation and regional conditions also affect its water balance. It was not simply a natural disappearance.
922|O‘zbekiston iqlimi asosan quruq kontinental: yoz issiq, qish esa hududga qarab sovuq bo‘lishi mumkin. Tog‘, vodiy va cho‘l sharoitlari farqlanadi; umumiy iqlim tavsifi ertangi ob-havo prognozi emas.|Uzbekistan has a largely dry continental climate, with hot summers and winters varying by region. Mountains, valleys and deserts differ; this general description is not a weather forecast.
925|Jahon merosi misollari: Xivadagi Ichan-qal’a, Buxoro tarixiy markazi va Samarqand — madaniyatlar chorrahasi. Bu to‘liq joriy ro‘yxat emas; yangi kiritishlar va mulk chegaralarini rasmiy ro‘yxatdan tekshirish kerak.|Examples are Itchan Kala, the Historic Centre of Bukhara and Samarkand—Crossroad of Cultures. This is not an exhaustive current list; additions and property boundaries require the official register.
926|Maydoni bo‘yicha eng katta okean — Tinch okeani. «Eng katta» deganda maydon, chuqurlik yoki hajm qaysi mezon ekani aniqlashtirilishi mumkin.|The Pacific is the largest ocean by area. For other comparisons, specify whether you mean area, depth or volume.
927|Materik odatda katta uzluksiz quruqlik massasiga, qit’a esa geografik-tarixiy tasnifga aytiladi. Tasnif an’anaga qarab farqlanadi: masalan, Yevropa va Osiyo bitta quruqlik massasida joylashgan.|A landmass and a continent are not always classified identically. Continental schemes vary by tradition; Europe and Asia share one continuous major landmass.
928|Dengiz sathidan balandlik bo‘yicha eng baland cho‘qqi — Everest (Jomolungma). Tagidan cho‘qqigacha balandlik yoki Yer markazidan uzoqlik boshqa mezon bo‘lib, boshqa natija berishi mumkin.|Everest is the highest summit above sea level. Height from base or distance from Earth’s centre are different measures and can produce different comparisons.
929|Qadimgi Misr Nil bo‘yidagi davlat tuzilishi, yozuv, piramidalar va diniy-madaniy merosi bilan tanilgan. Uning tarixi ming yillik davrlarni qamrab oladi; barchasini bitta hukmdor davriga tenglashtirmang.|Ancient Egypt is known for Nile-based state organisation, writing, pyramids and cultural/religious traditions. Its history spans millennia rather than a single ruler’s era.
930|Rim avval shahar-davlat, keyin respublika sifatida kengaydi. Respublikaning inqirozi va fuqarolar urushlaridan so‘ng Avgust davrida imperatorlik tartibi shakllandi. Bu bir kunda bo‘lgan oddiy nom almashtirish emas.|Rome expanded from a city-state into a republic. After republican crises and civil wars, imperial rule developed under Augustus, not merely through a one-day renaming.
931|Uyg‘onish davrida Yevropaning turli hududlarida antik merosga qiziqish, san’at, gumanistik ta’lim va ilmiy izlanish kuchaydi. Jarayon barcha hududda bir paytda yoki bir xil kechmagan.|The Renaissance involved renewed interest in classical learning, arts, humanistic education and inquiry in parts of Europe. It did not unfold identically or simultaneously everywhere.
932|Sanoat inqilobi ishlab chiqarishda mashinalar, energiya manbalari va zavod tizimining kengayishidir. Uning boshlanishida texnika, kapital, mehnat, bozorlar va institutlar kabi bir nechta omil qatnashgan; bitta sabab yetarli tushuntirish emas.|The Industrial Revolution expanded mechanised production, energy use and factory organisation. Technology, capital, labour, markets and institutions interacted; no single cause fully explains it.
933|Birinchi jahon urushi sabablarini ittifoqlar, qurollanish, imperiyalar raqobati va millatchilik kabi uzoq jarayonlardan ajrating. 1914-yildagi suiqasd va keyingi inqiroz bevosita qo‘zg‘atuvchi bo‘lgan, ammo yagona sabab emas.|Distinguish long-term alliances, armaments, imperial competition and nationalism from the assassination and diplomatic crisis of 1914, which triggered war but were not its only causes.
934|Ikkinchi jahon urushi 1945-yilda tugagan. Yevropadagi urush mayda, Yaponiya taslim bo‘lishining rasmiy hujjati esa 2-sentabrda imzolangan. Sana so‘ralganda qaysi front yoki hodisa nazarda tutilganini aniqlashtiring.|World War II ended in 1945. Fighting in Europe ended in May; Japan’s formal surrender was signed on 2 September. Specify the theatre or event when a precise date is required.
935|BMT 1945-yilda xalqaro tinchlik, xavfsizlik va hamkorlikni qo‘llab-quvvatlash maqsadida tashkil etilgan. Uning turli organlari vakolati har xil; u barcha davlatlar ustidan bitta jahon hukumati emas.|The United Nations was founded in 1945 to support international peace, security and cooperation. Its organs have different powers; it is not a single world government.
936|Yevropa Ittifoqi a’zo davlatlar o‘rtasidagi siyosiy va iqtisodiy ittifoqdir. U Yevropa qit’asi bilan bir xil emas; barcha Yevropa davlati uning a’zosi emas. Joriy a’zolik va qoidalar alohida tekshiriladi.|The European Union is a political and economic union of member states, not the same thing as the continent of Europe. Current membership and rules require separate verification.
937|Demokratiya siyosiy hokimiyatning xalq ishtiroki va hisobdorligi bilan bog‘liq boshqaruv tamoyilidir. Saylov, huquqlar, qonun ustuvorligi va institutlar muhim; faqat bitta ovoz berish hodisasi barcha shartlar bajarilganini isbotlamaydi.|Democracy connects political authority to public participation and accountability. Elections, rights, rule of law and institutions matter; a single vote does not establish every democratic condition.
938|Konstitutsiya davlatning asosiy boshqaruv tuzilishi, vakolatlar va huquqlar chegarasini belgilovchi asosiy huquqiy hujjatdir. Muayyan huquqiy masalada amaldagi matn va yurisdiksiya tekshirilishi kerak; bu individual yuridik maslahat emas.|A constitution establishes fundamental governance structures, powers and rights. A specific legal question requires the current text and jurisdiction; this definition is not individual legal advice.
942|Madina islom tarixida hijrat, dastlabki musulmon jamoasi va Masjid an-Nabaviy bilan muhim. Sayohat yoki ziyoratning joriy ruxsat va kirish qoidalarini alohida rasmiy tekshirish kerak.|Medina is important in Islamic history through the Hijra, early Muslim community and Prophet’s Mosque. Current travel and entry rules need separate official checks.
943|Makka islomda Ka’ba, haj va Muhammad payg‘ambarning ilk faoliyati bilan muhim bo‘lgan shahar. Tarixiy tavsif joriy ziyorat ruxsati yoki safar tartibini tasdiqlamaydi.|Mecca is central to Islam through the Kaaba, pilgrimage and the Prophet Muhammad’s early life. A historical description does not verify present pilgrimage or entry requirements.
944|Din tarixini xolis tushuntirishda e’tiqod tarafdorlarining qarashi, tarixiy dalil va olimlar talqinini ajrating. Qaysi din, davr yoki savolni solishtirmoqchisiz? Barcha an’anani bir xil deb yoki birining qarashini hamma uchun fakt deb ko‘rsatmayman.|For a neutral history, distinguish believers’ perspectives, historical evidence and scholarly interpretation. Which religion, period or question interests you? Different traditions should not be collapsed into one account.
945|Ramazon hijriy taqvimdagi oy bo‘lib, musulmonlar uchun ro‘za, ibodat va ehson bilan bog‘liq. Amaliy hukm yoki sog‘liq holatiga doir shaxsiy qaror uchun tegishli malakali mutaxassisga murojaat qilish kerak.|Ramadan is a month in the Islamic calendar associated with fasting, worship and charity. Individual religious rulings or health decisions require appropriate qualified guidance.
946|Hijriy taqvim oy harakatiga tayangan va yili milodiy quyosh yilidan qisqaroq. Shuning uchun hijriy oylar milodiy yil fasllari bo‘ylab siljiydi. Muayyan bayram sanasi uchun amaldagi rasmiy e’lonni tekshiring.|The Hijri calendar is lunar and its year is shorter than the Gregorian solar year, so its months move through the seasons. Check the applicable official announcement for a particular holiday date.
948|Ta’lim tizimini davomiylik, bosqichlar, kirish talabi, xarajat, malaka tan olinishi va amaliy natija bo‘yicha solishtiring. Bir reyting barcha o‘quvchiga moslikni aniqlamaydi. Qaysi davlatlar va qaysi bosqichni nazarda tutyapsiz?|Compare education systems by stages, duration, entry requirements, cost, recognition and outcomes. One ranking does not determine suitability for every learner. Which countries and level do you mean?
949|Besh muhim ilmiy rivojlanish misoli: mikroorganizmlarni kuzatish; elektromagnit hodisalarni tushuntirish; evolyutsion nazariya; DNK tuzilishini aniqlash; mikroblar va kasallik o‘rtasidagi aloqani tushunish. Ular ko‘p olim va tajriba hissasidan shakllangan, bittadan sodda «ixtirochi» bilan cheklanmaydi.|Examples include observing microorganisms, understanding electromagnetism, evolutionary theory, determining DNA structure and establishing links between microbes and disease. Each developed through contributions from many people and experiments.'''
